1
00:00:02,156 --> 00:00:04,595
(What a Happy Occasion)

2
00:00:04,596 --> 00:00:06,066
- Nice to see you all. - My gosh.

3
00:00:07,226 --> 00:00:09,465
- Congratulations are in order. - Yes.

4
00:00:09,466 --> 00:00:12,135
(Congratulations)

5
00:00:12,136 --> 00:00:13,735
- Is it someone's birthday? - What are we celebrating?

6
00:00:13,736 --> 00:00:14,765
- Our summer retreat episode... - Yes.

7
00:00:14,766 --> 00:00:16,176
aired last week,

8
00:00:16,276 --> 00:00:17,736
and our ratings were through the roof.

9
00:00:17,936 --> 00:00:18,936
We got good ratings.

10
00:00:18,937 --> 00:00:21,745
As for Ji Hyeon's team, Team Cooling Cooling,

11
00:00:21,746 --> 00:00:23,275
people wanted to see them on "Show! Music Core."

12
00:00:23,276 --> 00:00:24,315
- Really? - Yes.

13
00:00:24,316 --> 00:00:25,986
- There were so many comments. - Really?

14
00:00:26,546 --> 00:00:27,615
I'd love that.

15
00:00:27,616 --> 00:00:28,685
(Chuckling)

16
00:00:28,686 --> 00:00:30,885
- You sound like a grandpa. - That sounds amazing.

17
00:00:30,886 --> 00:00:32,626
There's one more thing for us to celebrate.

18
00:00:33,156 --> 00:00:34,456
It's the first for Moosquiat.

19
00:00:34,726 --> 00:00:37,296
You know the design I drew with the tablet PC for the T-shirts?

20
00:00:37,956 --> 00:00:40,766
(A group T-shirt to celebrate the summer retreat)

21
00:00:41,196 --> 00:00:42,296
T-shirts were sold out!

22
00:00:42,796 --> 00:00:44,436
- You can't buy it... - Sold out?

23
00:00:44,596 --> 00:00:46,135
- even if you want to now. - Gosh.

24
00:00:46,136 --> 00:00:47,436
Was it a limited edition?

25
00:00:47,506 --> 00:00:50,335
I was going to buy 100 shirts if no one bought them.

26
00:00:50,336 --> 00:00:51,336
- Okay. - Gosh.

27
00:00:51,337 --> 00:00:53,675
- I couldn't even buy them. - Gosh, what a surprise.

28
00:00:53,676 --> 00:00:55,276
(Laughing)

29
00:00:56,016 --> 00:00:57,915
(The Class of the Real Deal)

30
00:00:57,916 --> 00:00:59,345
"The Class of the Real Deal?"

31
00:00:59,346 --> 00:01:00,446
The Real Deal?

32
00:01:02,386 --> 00:01:03,655
(Art tools are scattered about.)

33
00:01:03,656 --> 00:01:04,886
It's an atelier.

34
00:01:05,256 --> 00:01:06,856
These tools look cool for some reason.

35
00:01:08,486 --> 00:01:10,956
(What are you doing?)

36
00:01:11,626 --> 00:01:13,695
(Painting)

37
00:01:13,696 --> 00:01:14,996
It's a new piece.

38
00:01:16,336 --> 00:01:17,865
(Kian84 is working on his artwork.)

39
00:01:17,866 --> 00:01:19,436
- He's the coolest when he paints. - Exactly.

40
00:01:19,836 --> 00:01:21,566
I've been working on my art.

41
00:01:23,006 --> 00:01:24,036
What's going on?

42
00:01:25,736 --> 00:01:30,246
(Someone has come to his atelier.)

43
00:01:31,446 --> 00:01:33,315
- Sir. - "Sir?"

44
00:01:33,316 --> 00:01:34,346
Sir.

45
00:01:36,256 --> 00:01:37,256
MINHO.

46
00:01:37,257 --> 00:01:38,555
(MINHO is visiting his atelier.)

47
00:01:38,556 --> 00:01:40,456
- You took MINHO. - MINHO?

48
00:01:41,156 --> 00:01:42,556
- I can't believe you're here. - Thank you for inviting me.

49
00:01:43,456 --> 00:01:44,495
Gosh, don't do that.

50
00:01:44,496 --> 00:01:46,496
He was on my team at the summer retreat.

51
00:01:47,026 --> 00:01:48,465
I brought kimchi to the retreat...

52
00:01:48,466 --> 00:01:49,836
and kimchi fried rice on the field day.

53
00:01:50,396 --> 00:01:53,236
I got the feeling that he was looking out for me.

54
00:01:53,536 --> 00:01:55,166
Right. He took good care of you.

55
00:01:56,836 --> 00:01:58,506
(Everyone was horrified by his kimchi fried rice.)

56
00:01:58,976 --> 00:02:00,575
(But I'm more curious about your effort than the taste.)

57
00:02:00,576 --> 00:02:01,905
That was almost a year ago.

58
00:02:01,906 --> 00:02:03,846
He still remembers that touching moment.

59
00:02:04,946 --> 00:02:08,686
(At the summer retreat, he brought plain cabbage kimchi.)

60
00:02:09,416 --> 00:02:10,955
(A series of compliments)

61
00:02:10,956 --> 00:02:12,686
He didn't compliment my anchovies.

62
00:02:13,786 --> 00:02:16,055
He's looking out for me.

63
00:02:16,056 --> 00:02:17,795
(He's grateful to MINHO and his attention.)

64
00:02:17,796 --> 00:02:19,126
(You're okay, right?)

65
00:02:19,626 --> 00:02:20,626
(It's okay, Kian84.)

66
00:02:20,996 --> 00:02:22,225
(It's okay that we lost.)

67
00:02:22,226 --> 00:02:24,236
(We still played better, though.)

68
00:02:24,366 --> 00:02:25,765
Thanks to people like him,

69
00:02:25,766 --> 00:02:27,865
school dropouts...

70
00:02:27,866 --> 00:02:29,935
- keep going. - What are you talking about?

71
00:02:29,936 --> 00:02:31,036
(He gives people courage, so they don't give up.)

72
00:02:31,276 --> 00:02:32,706
He could be the head of a department.

73
00:02:33,006 --> 00:02:34,405
But if he stops looking out for you,

74
00:02:34,406 --> 00:02:35,676
things easily get sour.

75
00:02:36,576 --> 00:02:38,115
Thanks to him, Kian84 didn't drop out.

76
00:02:38,116 --> 00:02:39,216
(I'll do better, MINHO.)

77
00:02:39,616 --> 00:02:42,415
I've always known that he likes to work out.

78
00:02:42,416 --> 00:02:44,316
Deep down, I felt like there was a connection between us.

79
00:02:46,356 --> 00:02:49,455
It thought it would be nice for us to pick a day and hang out.

80
00:02:49,456 --> 00:02:51,456
So I invited him to my atelier.

81
00:02:53,496 --> 00:02:54,526
Sir.

82
00:02:54,796 --> 00:02:56,166
- I can't believe you're here. - Thank you for inviting me.

83
00:02:57,166 --> 00:02:58,266
Gosh, don't do that.

84
00:02:59,096 --> 00:03:00,435
(Impressed)

85
00:03:00,436 --> 00:03:01,505
It doesn't look that good.

86
00:03:01,506 --> 00:03:02,706
(Shy)

87
00:03:02,906 --> 00:03:04,935
- This is amazing. - Gosh, don't say that.

88
00:03:04,936 --> 00:03:06,005
(Kian84 is working on a huge piece.)

89
00:03:06,006 --> 00:03:07,245
The colors look just beautiful.

90
00:03:07,246 --> 00:03:08,276
Right.

91
00:03:08,776 --> 00:03:10,315
This is ruined. I need to fix it.

92
00:03:10,316 --> 00:03:11,675
How is this ruined?

93
00:03:11,676 --> 00:03:12,786
My gosh.

94
00:03:13,346 --> 00:03:14,685
- It looks amazing. - Really?

95
00:03:14,686 --> 00:03:15,686
Yes.

96
00:03:15,687 --> 00:03:17,085
- It looks unrefined. - What?

97
00:03:17,086 --> 00:03:18,215
Gosh, stop it.

98
00:03:18,216 --> 00:03:20,326
- How does it look unrefined? - It just does.

99
00:03:20,856 --> 00:03:22,725
I was going to flip it around because I was too shy.

100
00:03:22,726 --> 00:03:24,095
- You'd never do that. - Since he came...

101
00:03:24,096 --> 00:03:25,226
Stop lying.

102
00:03:26,126 --> 00:03:28,596
I think you brought that from storage.

103
00:03:29,366 --> 00:03:31,096
- That wasn't there before. - Right.

104
00:03:31,696 --> 00:03:33,566
- Stop talking nonsense. - Well...

105
00:03:34,136 --> 00:03:36,005
No. It's not a finished piece, so I was shy to show it.

106
00:03:36,006 --> 00:03:37,436
But I left it in the open.

107
00:03:38,006 --> 00:03:39,845
What do you mean it looks unrefined?

108
00:03:39,846 --> 00:03:41,345
(Bombarding him with compliments as soon as he comes in)

109
00:03:41,346 --> 00:03:42,406
- Well... - Okay.

110
00:03:43,246 --> 00:03:44,545
(Raised cheeks)

111
00:03:44,546 --> 00:03:45,775
(Laughing)

112
00:03:45,776 --> 00:03:47,746
He's shy, but we have to compliment him.

113
00:03:47,916 --> 00:03:48,945
He likes that.

114
00:03:48,946 --> 00:03:51,186
(He's secretly enjoying the compliments.)

115
00:03:51,416 --> 00:03:53,885
It didn't feel right to come here empty-handed.

116
00:03:53,886 --> 00:03:55,685
- You invited me to your atelier. - Okay.

117
00:03:55,686 --> 00:03:57,256
- I brought a present. - You didn't have to.

118
00:03:57,396 --> 00:03:59,126
- My goodness. - He's got a big heart.

119
00:03:59,666 --> 00:04:02,096
- It's a recent hobby of mine. - Okay.

120
00:04:02,526 --> 00:04:04,896
I practiced bonsai a few times.

121
00:04:05,166 --> 00:04:07,236
(Amazed)

122
00:04:07,366 --> 00:04:08,665
- I... - This looks...

123
00:04:08,666 --> 00:04:10,606
repotted my plant into this one.

124
00:04:11,206 --> 00:04:12,206
Isn't it beautiful?

125
00:04:12,207 --> 00:04:14,105
I wanted to give this to you as a present.

126
00:04:14,106 --> 00:04:16,516
- Hey. - It's a new hobby of mine.

127
00:04:16,816 --> 00:04:19,246
Before that, my only hobby was working out.

128
00:04:19,646 --> 00:04:21,415
I thought I should try an activity...

129
00:04:21,416 --> 00:04:22,816
- that required me to be still. - Right.

130
00:04:23,156 --> 00:04:24,615
I recently tried it out.

131
00:04:24,616 --> 00:04:26,826
- And I actually liked it. - Right.

132
00:04:26,956 --> 00:04:28,685
I did think that it would be nice...

133
00:04:28,686 --> 00:04:30,396
for him to do a calming activity.

134
00:04:31,056 --> 00:04:32,496
- I bought a plant, - Okay.

135
00:04:32,796 --> 00:04:34,426
- so I could give it to you. - You made this?

136
00:04:34,896 --> 00:04:37,095
- I repotted it... - Okay.

137
00:04:37,096 --> 00:04:38,266
and trimmed it.

138
00:04:38,636 --> 00:04:39,905
You made it yourself?

139
00:04:39,906 --> 00:04:41,806
I also put moss on it myself.

140
00:04:42,776 --> 00:04:44,905
I thought this would make a nice present.

141
00:04:44,906 --> 00:04:46,075
- It looks beautiful. - Right.

142
00:04:46,076 --> 00:04:47,406
I always thought this looked cool.

143
00:04:48,076 --> 00:04:49,446
- Take good care of it. - Okay.

144
00:04:49,646 --> 00:04:51,216
- Thank you. - Don't mention it.

145
00:04:51,716 --> 00:04:52,846
- It looks great. - Right.

146
00:04:53,616 --> 00:04:55,446
Will this piece go to an exhibit?

147
00:04:56,046 --> 00:04:57,316
I have to.

148
00:04:57,716 --> 00:04:59,216
The moment I walked in,

149
00:04:59,886 --> 00:05:01,756
- I was overwhelmed by it. - Gosh.

150
00:05:02,126 --> 00:05:04,356
It instantly drew me in. I mean it.

151
00:05:04,696 --> 00:05:06,056
Kian84 must look different in there.

152
00:05:06,596 --> 00:05:09,996
It's more fascinating once it's on display at an exhibit.

153
00:05:10,436 --> 00:05:11,536
You're making me shy.

154
00:05:12,596 --> 00:05:14,765
(His cheeks are raised once again.)

155
00:05:14,766 --> 00:05:15,836
He likes that.

156
00:05:16,006 --> 00:05:18,205
Talking about this is making me shy.

157
00:05:18,206 --> 00:05:19,605
- Why? - I'm shy!

158
00:05:19,606 --> 00:05:21,705
(I'm shy!)

159
00:05:21,706 --> 00:05:23,316
You can't look him in the face.

160
00:05:23,546 --> 00:05:26,186
He kept complimenting me. I felt awkward.

161
00:05:27,386 --> 00:05:28,416
Wait.

162
00:05:29,316 --> 00:05:31,216
- It's 1pm. - It's 1pm?

163
00:05:31,856 --> 00:05:34,156
- Should we get going? - Right.

164
00:05:34,486 --> 00:05:35,625
Go where?

165
00:05:35,626 --> 00:05:37,455
Anyway, don't kill the plant.

166
00:05:37,456 --> 00:05:38,526
- I won't. - Okay.

167
00:05:38,856 --> 00:05:41,126
- I'll take it home. - Okay.

168
00:05:41,626 --> 00:05:44,036
Gosh, you startled me. I thought you were getting naked.

169
00:05:44,796 --> 00:05:47,065
I thought you weren't wearing anything underneath.

170
00:05:47,066 --> 00:05:48,206
My gosh. Hey.

171
00:05:48,436 --> 00:05:50,605
- Here. - Put it in here.

172
00:05:50,606 --> 00:05:51,606
My gosh.

173
00:05:51,607 --> 00:05:54,006
- Hey, did it cost a lot of money? - No, it didn't.

174
00:05:54,246 --> 00:05:55,375
Let's go.

175
00:05:55,376 --> 00:05:57,175
(Kian84 and MINHO go out.)

176
00:05:57,176 --> 00:05:58,246
Where are they going?

177
00:06:01,786 --> 00:06:03,116
I hope it doesn't rain.

178
00:06:03,586 --> 00:06:05,956
It's been raining quite frequently lately.

179
00:06:06,986 --> 00:06:09,185
Let's take my car.

180
00:06:09,186 --> 00:06:10,196
Let's go.

181
00:06:11,496 --> 00:06:12,726
My gosh.

182
00:06:13,126 --> 00:06:16,465
(They quickly get into his car.)

183
00:06:16,466 --> 00:06:17,596
What a cute car.

184
00:06:18,336 --> 00:06:20,805
- Let's get going. - Okay.

185
00:06:20,806 --> 00:06:22,566
(Glancing back)

186
00:06:22,806 --> 00:06:25,406
Gosh, there's only workout-related stuff in your car.

187
00:06:26,036 --> 00:06:28,375
I've never seen a wall ball in someone's car.

188
00:06:28,376 --> 00:06:29,875
Is this a car for a pro athlete?

189
00:06:29,876 --> 00:06:31,176
(It looks like an athlete's car.)

190
00:06:31,616 --> 00:06:34,346
(Setting out with his workout gear)

191
00:06:36,656 --> 00:06:37,755
(Rustling)

192
00:06:37,756 --> 00:06:40,286
- As long as we can do that... - Okay.

193
00:06:41,986 --> 00:06:44,256
- What's he doing? - What is he applying to his hair?

194
00:06:45,456 --> 00:06:46,696
Let me fix my hair.

195
00:06:47,166 --> 00:06:48,665
(Your hair?)

196
00:06:48,666 --> 00:06:49,966
I can do it with three ice cubes.

197
00:06:51,236 --> 00:06:52,266
Wait.

198
00:06:52,836 --> 00:06:54,965
- With the ice cubes from coffee? - Yes.

199
00:06:54,966 --> 00:06:56,035
Like beads.

200
00:06:56,036 --> 00:06:58,035
(Americano Hair)

201
00:06:58,036 --> 00:06:59,675
(He's washing his face while he's at it.)

202
00:06:59,676 --> 00:07:01,046
I always...

203
00:07:01,506 --> 00:07:03,976
- He suddenly took them out. - With the ice from coffee?

204
00:07:04,546 --> 00:07:07,246
I usually fix my hair with water.

205
00:07:07,646 --> 00:07:09,816
But I didn't have water, so I used the ice cubes.

206
00:07:10,416 --> 00:07:11,515
(Laughing)

207
00:07:11,516 --> 00:07:13,285
At the Blue Dragon Film Awards,

208
00:07:13,286 --> 00:07:14,655
they did a handprint event.

209
00:07:14,656 --> 00:07:16,625
Like some old guys at a rib restaurant,

210
00:07:16,626 --> 00:07:18,526
he used the wet towel to wipe his face.

211
00:07:19,766 --> 00:07:21,866
(At the Blue Dragon Film Awards,)

212
00:07:22,796 --> 00:07:25,395
(the camera was panning across...)

213
00:07:25,396 --> 00:07:26,906
(Stopping)

214
00:07:28,436 --> 00:07:30,306
(He didn't let it stop him and kept wiping his face.)

215
00:07:30,806 --> 00:07:32,706
("Kian84 Flusters Everyone with His Unexpected Action")

216
00:07:32,876 --> 00:07:34,505
- I wasn't going to do that. - You weren't?

217
00:07:34,506 --> 00:07:37,075
- Did you not wash your face? - I just can't help myself.

218
00:07:37,076 --> 00:07:38,346
You can't help yourself around wet towels?

219
00:07:38,646 --> 00:07:39,946
I have to do it.

220
00:07:40,186 --> 00:07:41,546
I had to style my hair and all.

221
00:07:42,016 --> 00:07:43,655
It's nice that the coffee didn't go to waste.

222
00:07:43,656 --> 00:07:44,685
(Clean84)

223
00:07:44,686 --> 00:07:46,885
I always try to look neat.

224
00:07:46,886 --> 00:07:49,426
Do you really style your hair with ice?

225
00:07:49,856 --> 00:07:51,126
No. I don't have water here.

226
00:07:51,596 --> 00:07:53,966
- He was styling himself. - I was styling myself.

227
00:07:54,826 --> 00:07:57,296
- Wait. You look neat now. - So...

228
00:07:59,166 --> 00:08:00,836
I look super neat afterward.

229
00:08:01,066 --> 00:08:03,636
Gosh, my hair smells like Americano.

230
00:08:03,936 --> 00:08:05,676
Exactly. I mean...

231
00:08:08,276 --> 00:08:11,145
Seriously. I'm an odd one, aren't I?

232
00:08:11,146 --> 00:08:12,916
(The savory aroma of coffee fills the car.)

233
00:08:13,316 --> 00:08:14,916
You're definitely one of a kind.

234
00:08:16,616 --> 00:08:17,816
Gosh, look at the weather.

235
00:08:18,716 --> 00:08:20,856
Actually, some rain would be nice.

236
00:08:21,056 --> 00:08:23,795
Right. I want it to pour down...

237
00:08:23,796 --> 00:08:25,025
instead of drizzling like this.

238
00:08:25,026 --> 00:08:26,426
I like running in the rain.

239
00:08:26,666 --> 00:08:28,426
- Running in the rain is fun. - Yes.

240
00:08:28,766 --> 00:08:30,635
- I like it. - What's your record for 10km?

241
00:08:30,636 --> 00:08:33,105
- What was your 1st record? - My 1st record was 45 minutes.

242
00:08:33,106 --> 00:08:34,965
- Your 1st record? - Yes. It was my 1st record.

243
00:08:34,966 --> 00:08:36,606
I can't believe you finished your 1st 10km run in 45 minutes.

244
00:08:36,836 --> 00:08:40,076
I want to help you get your PB.

245
00:08:40,146 --> 00:08:41,146
- Mine? - Yes.

246
00:08:41,147 --> 00:08:43,075
- Help me then. - So...

247
00:08:43,076 --> 00:08:44,615
- What's PB? - Personal Best.

248
00:08:44,616 --> 00:08:46,176
Your personal best record.

249
00:08:47,846 --> 00:08:49,016
They're going to a mountain.

250
00:08:49,646 --> 00:08:50,886
Are you guys hiking today?

251
00:08:52,086 --> 00:08:54,585
- We're here. - Thank you for driving us.

252
00:08:54,586 --> 00:08:56,526
(They arrive at the mountain-looking destination.)

253
00:08:57,426 --> 00:08:58,926
I hope it doesn't rain.

254
00:09:01,266 --> 00:09:02,496
Gosh, he set up his own here.

255
00:09:03,266 --> 00:09:04,595
- There. - I see tents over there.

256
00:09:04,596 --> 00:09:05,796
(Kian84 and MINHO spot something.)

257
00:09:08,306 --> 00:09:10,335
- Na Ra. - Na Ra.

258
00:09:10,336 --> 00:09:11,435
- Na Ra? - It's Na Ra.

259
00:09:11,436 --> 00:09:12,775
- Hey. - Wait.

260
00:09:12,776 --> 00:09:13,905
- You're here. - Hello.

261
00:09:13,906 --> 00:09:15,745
So for today's episode,

262
00:09:15,746 --> 00:09:17,745
I gathered some guys who genuinely love running.

263
00:09:17,746 --> 00:09:18,746
Okay.

264
00:09:18,747 --> 00:09:21,845
I wanted to show you what proper running looked like.

265
00:09:21,846 --> 00:09:23,316
- The proper running? - Yes.

266
00:09:23,986 --> 00:09:26,016
You're such a turncoat.

267
00:09:26,626 --> 00:09:27,955
- You... - Hey.

268
00:09:27,956 --> 00:09:29,186
Hyun Moo is mad for real.

269
00:09:29,556 --> 00:09:30,556
Hyun Moo.

270
00:09:30,557 --> 00:09:32,355
I've never seen him this charismatic before.

271
00:09:32,356 --> 00:09:34,996
Na Ra is suddenly getting thirsty.

272
00:09:35,396 --> 00:09:38,136
(Na Ra was a member of the Fun Run Crew.)

273
00:09:39,536 --> 00:09:41,265
Gosh. That's true!

274
00:09:41,266 --> 00:09:42,465
(Transferring to the Proper Run Crew)

275
00:09:42,466 --> 00:09:44,105
Well, that's how life works.

276
00:09:44,106 --> 00:09:46,605
I was just camping there. And they showed up there.

277
00:09:46,606 --> 00:09:48,406
(That's the excuse he comes up with.)

278
00:09:48,476 --> 00:09:49,545
- Hyun Moo. - Ji Hyeon won't walk out...

279
00:09:49,546 --> 00:09:50,646
from the adjacent tent, right?

280
00:09:51,516 --> 00:09:52,915
- "Hey!" - Gosh, no.

281
00:09:52,916 --> 00:09:54,686
- Ji Hyeon, you can't switch. - I don't do that.

282
00:09:55,746 --> 00:09:57,585
- What do you mean? - He's disappointed.

283
00:09:57,586 --> 00:09:58,615
- You're making Na Ra look bad. - You won't do that?

284
00:09:58,616 --> 00:10:00,756
Wait. You want to run fast now?

285
00:10:01,286 --> 00:10:02,886
(He has no excuse to offer now.)

286
00:10:03,156 --> 00:10:04,326
You're here.

287
00:10:04,596 --> 00:10:05,826
- Hello. - Gosh.

288
00:10:05,926 --> 00:10:07,966
- Hello. Gosh. - Hello.

289
00:10:08,166 --> 00:10:10,636
- Come on. What is this? - Hey.

290
00:10:10,796 --> 00:10:12,495
- You're already sweating. - Yes.

291
00:10:12,496 --> 00:10:13,905
- Thank you for doing everything. - It rained...

292
00:10:13,906 --> 00:10:14,965
- Okay. - when I was pitching the tent.

293
00:10:14,966 --> 00:10:16,606
- Right. - Yes.

294
00:10:17,806 --> 00:10:18,875
(It poured down when he was pitching the tent.)

295
00:10:18,876 --> 00:10:20,475
It poured down...

296
00:10:20,476 --> 00:10:22,045
- when I was pitching the tent. - That serves you right.

297
00:10:22,046 --> 00:10:24,576
(That serves you right.)

298
00:10:26,116 --> 00:10:27,285
It's like a scene in a drama.

299
00:10:27,286 --> 00:10:29,615
(He finishes setting it up while getting drenched in rain.)

300
00:10:29,616 --> 00:10:31,416
I didn't know he had to do it in the rain.

301
00:10:31,656 --> 00:10:34,155
My gosh. But that must've been a lot of work.

302
00:10:34,156 --> 00:10:35,386
That's not easy.

303
00:10:35,956 --> 00:10:38,356
Gosh, look at your outfit.

304
00:10:38,896 --> 00:10:40,495
What? No, you don't have to do that.

305
00:10:40,496 --> 00:10:41,895
It was a long trip, wasn't it?

306
00:10:41,896 --> 00:10:44,996
No, we got here faster than we thought. Talking about running...

307
00:10:45,336 --> 00:10:48,065
I saw him paint a bit in his atelier.

308
00:10:48,066 --> 00:10:49,706
- Really? - Yes.

309
00:10:50,106 --> 00:10:51,135
We were in my atelier for a bit.

310
00:10:51,136 --> 00:10:52,705
- Really? - Why... You startled me.

311
00:10:52,706 --> 00:10:53,905
- What? You suddenly... - What are you doing?

312
00:10:53,906 --> 00:10:56,406
- Hold on. You're doing that a lot. - Really?

313
00:10:56,446 --> 00:10:57,715
(He's taking off his clothes again?)

314
00:10:57,716 --> 00:10:58,875
- You keep stripping. - Come on, Kian84.

315
00:10:58,876 --> 00:11:00,385
- I'm getting ready to run. - You took off your suit earlier...

316
00:11:00,386 --> 00:11:01,416
and now your pants.

317
00:11:01,486 --> 00:11:03,616
- He did the same thing earlier. - Really?

318
00:11:04,016 --> 00:11:05,286
- You know what? - Yes.

319
00:11:05,386 --> 00:11:08,886
Let's give today a try. If we make a good team,

320
00:11:09,386 --> 00:11:12,256
let's try the 10km marathon together.

321
00:11:13,826 --> 00:11:15,726
- I love it. - Okay.

322
00:11:15,926 --> 00:11:17,196
We could do so many things as runners.

323
00:11:17,696 --> 00:11:19,366
I always ask MINHO.

324
00:11:19,496 --> 00:11:21,066
"How many kilometers do you run?"

325
00:11:21,666 --> 00:11:23,065
"What have you been doing for your exercise lately?"

326
00:11:23,066 --> 00:11:24,376
As we discussed this a lot,

327
00:11:24,536 --> 00:11:28,706
we decided to pick a day and go for a run together.

328
00:11:29,176 --> 00:11:31,016
MINHO and I planned it.

329
00:11:31,376 --> 00:11:33,175
Just like I asked many questions to MINHO,

330
00:11:33,176 --> 00:11:35,016
this guy asked me many questions.

331
00:11:35,346 --> 00:11:38,056
It was Na Ra.

332
00:11:38,756 --> 00:11:40,386
(In the car during the summer retreat)

333
00:11:41,286 --> 00:11:43,756
(I always run alone.)

334
00:11:44,126 --> 00:11:47,566
(Sometimes, it gets boring.)

335
00:11:48,296 --> 00:11:50,436
(Let's run together.)

336
00:11:50,996 --> 00:11:53,866
(He appealed to Kian84 with his passion for running.)

337
00:11:54,606 --> 00:11:56,235
Then I thought the three of us should do it.

338
00:11:56,236 --> 00:11:58,306
So the three of us ended up coming here for a run.

339
00:11:59,876 --> 00:12:03,106
(The eldest and crew chief, Kian84)

340
00:12:04,216 --> 00:12:07,416
(He doesn't stop running even in extreme conditions.)

341
00:12:08,616 --> 00:12:11,015
- Gosh, he's so fast. - That was just crazy.

342
00:12:11,016 --> 00:12:12,885
(He participated in the HYROX Taipei event.)

343
00:12:12,886 --> 00:12:14,055
- Gosh. - He's just on another level.

344
00:12:14,056 --> 00:12:16,025
- He won 1st place. - He won 1st place.

345
00:12:16,026 --> 00:12:17,725
- That was just crazy. - That's...

346
00:12:17,726 --> 00:12:18,826
He won first place in Asia.

347
00:12:19,456 --> 00:12:20,765
(He built his stamina through regular routines.)

348
00:12:20,766 --> 00:12:21,895
He's a comedian.

349
00:12:21,896 --> 00:12:23,166
(He built his stamina through regular routines.)

350
00:12:23,936 --> 00:12:29,636
(Energizer Na Ra with endless energy)

351
00:12:31,106 --> 00:12:32,576
I thought, "It's finally happening."

352
00:12:32,836 --> 00:12:36,676
I tend to put a lot of emphasis on the beginning.

353
00:12:37,376 --> 00:12:38,746
Like your first crush.

354
00:12:39,146 --> 00:12:40,845
- Or... - This is making me want to vomit.

355
00:12:40,846 --> 00:12:43,686
your first experiences.

356
00:12:43,886 --> 00:12:45,155
I value them a lot.

357
00:12:45,156 --> 00:12:48,386
And running with Kian84 for the 1st time...

358
00:12:48,986 --> 00:12:50,355
really excited me.

359
00:12:50,356 --> 00:12:52,596
So I had trouble going to sleep.

360
00:12:52,796 --> 00:12:55,195
- I was that excited. - Gosh, really? It's just a run.

361
00:12:55,196 --> 00:12:56,196
(Shy)

362
00:12:56,696 --> 00:12:58,436
(Eyes closed)

363
00:12:58,536 --> 00:12:59,636
I was touched.

364
00:13:00,636 --> 00:13:02,136
I wanted to run with Kian84.

365
00:13:02,936 --> 00:13:04,136
I like Kian84.

366
00:13:05,636 --> 00:13:09,605
I actually picked up running...

367
00:13:09,606 --> 00:13:11,615
after watching Kian84.

368
00:13:11,616 --> 00:13:14,686
- My gosh. They weren't meant to be. - His TV shows...

369
00:13:15,046 --> 00:13:17,186
- I really liked your TV shows. - Thank you.

370
00:13:17,556 --> 00:13:18,956
I watched all of his shows.

371
00:13:19,256 --> 00:13:22,456
As a runner, he was my role model.

372
00:13:23,026 --> 00:13:25,756
And being asked to run with him...

373
00:13:27,196 --> 00:13:29,395
made me so happy and emotional even.

374
00:13:29,396 --> 00:13:30,635
Gosh. You were that happy?

375
00:13:30,636 --> 00:13:31,966
(Smiling)

376
00:13:32,396 --> 00:13:33,605
- We can go abroad... - Yes.

377
00:13:33,606 --> 00:13:35,506
and run with the crew there.

378
00:13:36,206 --> 00:13:38,335
- We could do a lot with running. - There are so many things to do.

379
00:13:38,336 --> 00:13:40,446
- So I heard about your age. - Yes.

380
00:13:40,506 --> 00:13:41,645
You were born in 1990?

381
00:13:41,646 --> 00:13:44,045
I was born in early 1991.

382
00:13:44,046 --> 00:13:45,676
All of my friends were born in 1990.

383
00:13:46,176 --> 00:13:48,115
Are you more comfortable if I address you as an older brother?

384
00:13:48,116 --> 00:13:50,285
- Whatever you feel comfortable. - It doesn't matter to me at all.

385
00:13:50,286 --> 00:13:51,686
- Really? - Wait.

386
00:13:52,156 --> 00:13:53,316
Then...

387
00:13:53,626 --> 00:13:56,255
- I was born on December 9, 1991. - December 9.

388
00:13:56,256 --> 00:13:58,895
- I was born in January. - Then we're almost 11 months apart.

389
00:13:58,896 --> 00:14:00,265
So we're almost a year apart.

390
00:14:00,266 --> 00:14:02,595
- Treat me as an older brother. - Yes, you are.

391
00:14:02,596 --> 00:14:03,765
My brother, Na Ra.

392
00:14:03,766 --> 00:14:05,896
I should've done that from the get-go.

393
00:14:06,236 --> 00:14:07,965
- That's more comfortable for me. - The social titles got messed up.

394
00:14:07,966 --> 00:14:09,205
(Joking)

395
00:14:09,206 --> 00:14:10,706
Seriously.

396
00:14:10,876 --> 00:14:12,775
Will you... Wait. Will he know after today?

397
00:14:12,776 --> 00:14:14,106
If the Fun Run is better for him?

398
00:14:14,446 --> 00:14:16,545
- Besides, - Once he does a proper run?

399
00:14:16,546 --> 00:14:19,316
the Fun Run Crew is all fake.

400
00:14:19,476 --> 00:14:20,986
- That's true. - It's all fake.

401
00:14:21,386 --> 00:14:23,585
- Well... - You were deceived.

402
00:14:23,586 --> 00:14:24,786
- They used you. - He's gaslighting Na Ra.

403
00:14:25,516 --> 00:14:27,756
How fast did you run? Did it take 20 minutes to run 1km?

404
00:14:27,886 --> 00:14:30,355
It was over 20 minutes.

405
00:14:30,356 --> 00:14:32,196
- Was it 26 minutes? - It was 26 minutes?

406
00:14:32,296 --> 00:14:34,596
What do you think about taking 26 minutes to run 1km?

407
00:14:36,266 --> 00:14:40,366
(Jogging lightly, so their knees don't hurt)

408
00:14:41,036 --> 00:14:44,735
(They freely ate and hung out while running.)

409
00:14:44,736 --> 00:14:45,876
He had so much fun.

410
00:14:48,006 --> 00:14:51,216
(Happiness was more important than records for the Fun Run Crew.)

411
00:14:52,016 --> 00:14:54,686
Bring that T-shirt back next week.

412
00:14:57,256 --> 00:14:58,515
- You must return it. - I thought he could keep it.

413
00:14:58,516 --> 00:14:59,615
- He can't keep it? - No, he can't.

414
00:14:59,616 --> 00:15:01,185
Oh, no. He's sad. His eyes are wet.

415
00:15:01,186 --> 00:15:02,686
- Right. - His eyes are getting wet.

416
00:15:03,926 --> 00:15:05,496
(Teary)

417
00:15:05,796 --> 00:15:06,995
You have the physique of a good runner.

418
00:15:06,996 --> 00:15:09,696
- His body is built to hit a low 40. - Look at his ankles.

419
00:15:09,796 --> 00:15:11,295
- At the competitions, - Okay.

420
00:15:11,296 --> 00:15:13,265
there's a category for skilled amateurs.

421
00:15:13,266 --> 00:15:15,405
And those runners have a specific build.

422
00:15:15,406 --> 00:15:17,076
- And you have the same build. - He's one of them.

423
00:15:17,676 --> 00:15:20,946
Na Ra looks like a magazine model for a running brand.

424
00:15:21,076 --> 00:15:23,176
- He's got that build. - Seriously. His figure...

425
00:15:23,946 --> 00:15:25,675
- Should we start running? - Let's go.

426
00:15:25,676 --> 00:15:27,385
I'll go inside and change.

427
00:15:27,386 --> 00:15:28,486
Okay.

428
00:15:28,746 --> 00:15:31,516
- You can change here. - It doesn't matter.

429
00:15:31,986 --> 00:15:33,256
All right. Let's warm up.

430
00:15:34,456 --> 00:15:36,486
- Just the ankles. - Let's do some taping.

431
00:15:36,996 --> 00:15:38,325
I'll tape only my ankles.

432
00:15:38,326 --> 00:15:40,696
(I'll tape only my ankles.)

433
00:15:42,096 --> 00:15:46,066
- My ankles weakened a bit. - Hey.

434
00:15:46,196 --> 00:15:47,405
This is...

435
00:15:47,406 --> 00:15:49,006
- The ligament? - Yes, my ligament.

436
00:15:51,236 --> 00:15:53,476
- But... - Gosh, this is nice.

437
00:15:54,076 --> 00:15:55,705
I think taping does help.

438
00:15:55,706 --> 00:15:56,746
(The crew chief personally puts on tapes on his ankles.)

439
00:15:57,046 --> 00:15:58,616
Do you have a warm-up routine?

440
00:15:58,716 --> 00:16:00,446
- I'll follow yours. - I have one.

441
00:16:00,646 --> 00:16:01,646
- Here it goes. - Okay.

442
00:16:01,647 --> 00:16:02,845
- Circle your wrists and ankles. - Wrists and ankles.

443
00:16:02,846 --> 00:16:04,015
One, two,

444
00:16:04,016 --> 00:16:07,426
three, four, five, six, seven.

445
00:16:07,856 --> 00:16:09,585
- One, two. - One, two.

446
00:16:09,586 --> 00:16:11,055
- One, two. Two. - Two.

447
00:16:11,056 --> 00:16:12,525
- One, two, three. - Three.

448
00:16:12,526 --> 00:16:13,925
- One, two, three, four. - Gosh.

449
00:16:13,926 --> 00:16:15,195
- One, two, three. - They could keep up very well.

450
00:16:15,196 --> 00:16:16,525
- Five. - One, two, three.

451
00:16:16,526 --> 00:16:19,866
- Six. - Two, three, four,

452
00:16:20,536 --> 00:16:22,136
- five, six. - Five.

453
00:16:22,306 --> 00:16:23,366
My heart rate is up.

454
00:16:24,006 --> 00:16:25,705
I thought that was a bad thing.

455
00:16:25,706 --> 00:16:27,875
- It should be elevated a bit. - No, that's a good thing.

456
00:16:27,876 --> 00:16:29,306
- We need to get the blood flowing. - Yes.

457
00:16:29,406 --> 00:16:30,516
It's exhausting.

458
00:16:31,416 --> 00:16:33,115
Let's get going now.

459
00:16:33,116 --> 00:16:34,546
I don't know where we're going.

460
00:16:34,746 --> 00:16:36,856
- We're going to start here. - Okay.

461
00:16:37,086 --> 00:16:40,426
It was the first time I was running with MINHO...

462
00:16:40,756 --> 00:16:42,186
and Na Ra.

463
00:16:42,486 --> 00:16:45,255
Instead of running in the city, I wanted us to do trail running.

464
00:16:45,256 --> 00:16:46,296
It would be different.

465
00:16:46,626 --> 00:16:49,925
- Trailing running is a mix... - My gosh.

466
00:16:49,926 --> 00:16:51,366
of hiking and marathons.

467
00:16:51,966 --> 00:16:53,166
They're running on mountains.

468
00:16:53,666 --> 00:16:57,106
I did that when I trained as a judo player.

469
00:16:57,276 --> 00:16:59,106
I woke up at 4am every day.

470
00:17:00,036 --> 00:17:02,276
I stretched and then went up to the mountain.

471
00:17:02,606 --> 00:17:04,675
Track and field athletes do that. Right?

472
00:17:04,676 --> 00:17:06,445
You go up to the top and then come back down.

473
00:17:06,446 --> 00:17:07,586
You're one of us then.

474
00:17:07,816 --> 00:17:08,946
My gosh.

475
00:17:10,186 --> 00:17:12,456
- She was young back then. - Thinking about that...

476
00:17:12,756 --> 00:17:14,585
still makes me feel dizzy. Seriously.

477
00:17:14,586 --> 00:17:15,686
Right.

478
00:17:16,386 --> 00:17:19,296
Running on mountains will be really tough.

479
00:17:19,896 --> 00:17:23,026
So afterward, it improves your record on flatland.

480
00:17:23,426 --> 00:17:26,266
Avid runners do a lot of trail running.

481
00:17:26,596 --> 00:17:29,236
- It's like a new genre. - It's a training exercise.

482
00:17:30,776 --> 00:17:32,836
We're at Mount Ilja.

483
00:17:32,936 --> 00:17:34,946
Mount Ilja. I guess it's straight.

484
00:17:35,446 --> 00:17:37,275
This is a very popular mountain...

485
00:17:37,276 --> 00:17:39,416
for trail runners.

486
00:17:40,786 --> 00:17:42,946
Lee Bong Ju also used to run here a lot.

487
00:17:43,516 --> 00:17:46,286
A lot of enthusiastic runners go to that mountain.

488
00:17:48,786 --> 00:17:52,196
We're going to set out from the campsite and go up.

489
00:17:52,326 --> 00:17:54,026
Then we'll come to our first turning point.

490
00:17:54,296 --> 00:17:56,125
We'll keep running.

491
00:17:56,126 --> 00:17:58,996
Past the summit, we'll reach the second turning point.

492
00:17:59,196 --> 00:18:02,136
From there, we'll return to the campsite.

493
00:18:03,006 --> 00:18:06,806
Then the total distance of the trail run will be 7.8km.

494
00:18:07,746 --> 00:18:09,305
What kind of shape is that?

495
00:18:09,306 --> 00:18:10,445
Because people name the run after the shape?

496
00:18:10,446 --> 00:18:11,975
- It looks like a dustpan. - What?

497
00:18:11,976 --> 00:18:13,115
- Don't say that. - A dustpan?

498
00:18:13,116 --> 00:18:14,585
- The Dustpan Run. - I haven't heard that in a while.

499
00:18:14,586 --> 00:18:16,385
- The Dustpan Run. - That's the most infuriating.

500
00:18:16,386 --> 00:18:17,615
(Talking about the shape is the most infuriating.)

501
00:18:17,616 --> 00:18:19,116
I hate that.

502
00:18:19,386 --> 00:18:21,386
I only had the shape of the whale in my head.

503
00:18:22,156 --> 00:18:24,056
- The whale? - I'm determined to crush the whale.

504
00:18:24,126 --> 00:18:25,126
(Sad)

505
00:18:25,127 --> 00:18:26,396
Catch the whale.

506
00:18:27,066 --> 00:18:29,196
I really liked it.

507
00:18:29,996 --> 00:18:33,296
Once you're good at trail running, you'll be good at road running.

508
00:18:33,596 --> 00:18:35,605
I wanted us to have fun with the run today.

509
00:18:35,606 --> 00:18:36,975
That's what I thought when we began.

510
00:18:36,976 --> 00:18:38,836
I don't see any excitement in your eyes.

511
00:18:39,806 --> 00:18:42,476
- I was determined that day. - Seriously. You look so determined.

512
00:18:43,446 --> 00:18:45,576
I was quite serious about it too.

513
00:18:45,916 --> 00:18:46,946
I was quite serious.

514
00:18:47,486 --> 00:18:50,385
It felt like the battlefield of men...

515
00:18:50,386 --> 00:18:52,916
who gathered to do some real running.

516
00:18:53,116 --> 00:18:54,956
(Disappointed)

517
00:18:55,986 --> 00:18:57,556
- Let's go. We got this. - Okay. Let's go. We got this.

518
00:19:01,196 --> 00:19:03,766
We started running in the most serious manner.

519
00:19:04,096 --> 00:19:06,895
The three of us didn't talk. We were quiet.

520
00:19:06,896 --> 00:19:09,635
- Yes. We were quiet. - That's how we started our run.

521
00:19:09,636 --> 00:19:12,206
- Right. We focused on its essence. - We focused on its essence.

522
00:19:12,676 --> 00:19:14,775
- We didn't have to be chatty. - Right.

523
00:19:14,776 --> 00:19:15,776
- We didn't do that. - We just...

524
00:19:15,777 --> 00:19:17,176
You guys are the chattiest right now.

525
00:19:19,046 --> 00:19:20,515
- We didn't talk then. - We focused on its essence.

526
00:19:20,516 --> 00:19:22,246
- So we're talking now. - Right.

527
00:19:23,186 --> 00:19:26,515
(The Proper Run Crew enters the trail course.)

528
00:19:26,516 --> 00:19:27,886
- Gosh. - By the way,

529
00:19:29,126 --> 00:19:30,495
it's nice that there are trees.

530
00:19:30,496 --> 00:19:32,025
- Yes. It's nice and cool. - Yes.

531
00:19:32,026 --> 00:19:33,995
This is the upside of trail running. Looking at the scenery...

532
00:19:33,996 --> 00:19:35,295
doesn't get boring.

533
00:19:35,296 --> 00:19:36,396
(Looking at the scenery is one of the perks.)

534
00:19:38,066 --> 00:19:39,165
(MINHO is running slightly ahead of them.)

535
00:19:39,166 --> 00:19:40,965
MINHO wants to run a bit faster.

536
00:19:40,966 --> 00:19:42,036
- Right. - I bet.

537
00:19:42,236 --> 00:19:44,206
I bet there's a bit of rivalry between MINHO and Kian84.

538
00:19:44,236 --> 00:19:47,076
What rivalry? He's my crew chief.

539
00:19:48,176 --> 00:19:52,776
(Retching)

540
00:19:53,816 --> 00:19:55,816
(Glancing)

541
00:19:55,946 --> 00:19:58,656
- Gosh, I love this trail. - It's cool.

542
00:20:00,686 --> 00:20:02,025
With trail running,

543
00:20:02,026 --> 00:20:03,356
- we can admire the view. - Right.

544
00:20:04,396 --> 00:20:06,525
It's a different vibe from the road.

545
00:20:06,526 --> 00:20:09,126
The scent of grass definitely improves your mood.

546
00:20:10,736 --> 00:20:12,536
- I love this trail. - Yes.

547
00:20:12,696 --> 00:20:15,235
Especially during summer when the sun is too strong,

548
00:20:15,236 --> 00:20:17,676
- it's cooler in the mountains. - There are shaded areas too.

549
00:20:17,736 --> 00:20:19,406
- Mountains are better. - They are.

550
00:20:19,606 --> 00:20:20,746
Staying home is better.

551
00:20:21,206 --> 00:20:23,275
- Right. You do have a point. - It's cool in the house.

552
00:20:23,276 --> 00:20:24,315
True.

553
00:20:24,316 --> 00:20:25,916
I hope the course stays flat.

554
00:20:26,016 --> 00:20:27,216
If it's flat like this...

555
00:20:28,316 --> 00:20:29,446
- It'd be perfect. - Yes.

556
00:20:30,986 --> 00:20:33,955
- Gosh. We should be careful here. - Be careful.

557
00:20:33,956 --> 00:20:37,056
(They enter the mountainous path.)

558
00:20:38,156 --> 00:20:40,295
Man, there's an uphill already.

559
00:20:40,296 --> 00:20:41,596
Gosh, there's an uphill right away.

560
00:20:42,726 --> 00:20:44,096
With this kind of uphill...

561
00:20:45,866 --> 00:20:48,105
I usually run slower. Actually, this pace...

562
00:20:48,106 --> 00:20:49,506
- Okay. - is quite fast.

563
00:20:49,736 --> 00:20:52,275
We can take it slow.

564
00:20:52,276 --> 00:20:53,305
(They run, following MINHO's lead.)

565
00:20:53,306 --> 00:20:54,375
We got this.

566
00:20:54,376 --> 00:20:55,776
(We got this.)

567
00:20:59,316 --> 00:21:00,545
You should go in front.

568
00:21:00,546 --> 00:21:01,946
(A narrow path)

569
00:21:03,546 --> 00:21:05,116
- Gosh, be careful. - Oh, stairs.

570
00:21:05,356 --> 00:21:07,015
- Oh, it's mud. - Mud.

571
00:21:07,016 --> 00:21:08,326
(A muddy trail)

572
00:21:08,626 --> 00:21:10,325
- Be careful. - It rained that morning.

573
00:21:10,326 --> 00:21:12,026
- So the path was slippery. - Oh, no.

574
00:21:16,626 --> 00:21:17,766
Gosh, the excruciating stairs.

575
00:21:18,336 --> 00:21:19,465
(After the muddy path, they enter the excruciating stairs.)

576
00:21:19,466 --> 00:21:20,865
- Be careful. - We're done for.

577
00:21:20,866 --> 00:21:22,935
- Oh, my. It's endless. - What is this?

578
00:21:22,936 --> 00:21:25,835
The first stretch of the trail was pretty steep.

579
00:21:25,836 --> 00:21:27,006
Oh, my.

580
00:21:34,616 --> 00:21:37,486
(Silence fills the air with the endless stairs.)

581
00:21:37,856 --> 00:21:39,485
(Campsite, Turning Point 1, Turning Point 2)

582
00:21:39,486 --> 00:21:43,896
(Campsite, Turning Point 1)

583
00:21:45,226 --> 00:21:48,896
(The members of the Proper Run Crew run up the endless stairs.)

584
00:21:49,396 --> 00:21:51,936
(Taking off his cap)

585
00:21:53,336 --> 00:21:57,206
(Panting)

586
00:21:57,506 --> 00:21:59,776
- Gosh, I love these stairs. - Oh, my.

587
00:22:00,976 --> 00:22:03,146
MINHO kept on running up without getting tired.

588
00:22:03,346 --> 00:22:05,946
Gosh, MINHO is just getting started.

589
00:22:09,246 --> 00:22:13,285
(The crew chief is leading his crew in the front.)

590
00:22:13,286 --> 00:22:14,456
- MINHO, you go first. - Okay.

591
00:22:15,386 --> 00:22:17,725
(The stairs are slowing the older members down.)

592
00:22:17,726 --> 00:22:19,026
Should we go slower?

593
00:22:19,556 --> 00:22:21,996
- Hey. No. Keep going. - Okay.

594
00:22:23,326 --> 00:22:24,966
The stairs are endless.

595
00:22:25,436 --> 00:22:26,496
This is crazy.

596
00:22:27,906 --> 00:22:28,966
Is this for real?

597
00:22:29,436 --> 00:22:30,976
This is how trail running goes.

598
00:22:31,476 --> 00:22:33,076
- This is the hard part. - This is trail running?

599
00:22:33,336 --> 00:22:34,506
This is trail running.

600
00:22:35,146 --> 00:22:38,176
(As he runs up the endless stairs,)

601
00:22:38,346 --> 00:22:43,046
(Na Ra is starting to get tired.)

602
00:22:45,286 --> 00:22:46,585
(Glancing back)

603
00:22:46,586 --> 00:22:48,486
- MINHO, you're not even panting. - Yes? What?

604
00:22:48,526 --> 00:22:51,025
- You're breathing, right? - My breathing is pretty good.

605
00:22:51,026 --> 00:22:52,696
(Stopping)

606
00:22:52,756 --> 00:22:54,125
- I knew it. - Let's walk here for a bit.

607
00:22:54,126 --> 00:22:56,226
Let's walk. Okay.

608
00:22:58,296 --> 00:23:00,605
That's different from running.

609
00:23:00,606 --> 00:23:01,705
- Right. - It's so different.

610
00:23:01,706 --> 00:23:02,736
Exactly.

611
00:23:03,066 --> 00:23:06,136
(Only the sounds of heavy breathing fill the air.)

612
00:23:06,206 --> 00:23:07,245
Hey.

613
00:23:07,246 --> 00:23:08,275
(Look at that.)

614
00:23:08,276 --> 00:23:11,145
What is it? One hundred eight? One hundred eighty?

615
00:23:11,146 --> 00:23:12,545
(His heart rate is at 180.)

616
00:23:12,546 --> 00:23:14,486
- My gosh. - Oh, my.

617
00:23:14,546 --> 00:23:15,685
Call an ambulance.

618
00:23:15,686 --> 00:23:17,215
(Joking)

619
00:23:17,216 --> 00:23:19,285
It's dangerous if your heart rate goes over 180.

620
00:23:19,286 --> 00:23:20,486
You should slow down.

621
00:23:20,626 --> 00:23:22,285
- Actually, - He has to stop.

622
00:23:22,286 --> 00:23:24,295
when you want to hit a personal best,

623
00:23:24,296 --> 00:23:26,195
it has to hover around 190.

624
00:23:26,196 --> 00:23:27,325
- Hover around there? - Was that the dead point?

625
00:23:27,326 --> 00:23:28,766
- It was the dead point. - It is.

626
00:23:29,096 --> 00:23:30,126
I didn't know.

627
00:23:31,096 --> 00:23:32,735
(They finally finish climbing up the stairs.)

628
00:23:32,736 --> 00:23:33,866
Gosh. I...

629
00:23:35,066 --> 00:23:36,306
I'm not in shape.

630
00:23:36,766 --> 00:23:39,536
- Mine went up to 160. - How's your breathing?

631
00:23:40,536 --> 00:23:41,805
Eight minutes and fifty-six seconds.

632
00:23:41,806 --> 00:23:43,075
(Campsite, Turning Point 1, Turning Point 2)

633
00:23:43,076 --> 00:23:46,075
It was quite hilly. So our pace is pretty good.

634
00:23:46,076 --> 00:23:47,746
(Campsite, Turning Point 1, Turning Point 2)

635
00:23:48,316 --> 00:23:49,985
- It's a downhill. - Yes.

636
00:23:49,986 --> 00:23:51,356
Recovery.

637
00:23:51,486 --> 00:23:53,616
- Now, when you run, - Recovery.

638
00:23:54,326 --> 00:23:55,656
don't tense up your legs.

639
00:23:56,156 --> 00:23:57,226
Focus on your toes.

640
00:23:57,356 --> 00:23:59,196
- Put weight on our toes. Great. - Recovery.

641
00:23:59,656 --> 00:24:01,396
An uphill is always followed by a downhill.

642
00:24:02,766 --> 00:24:04,166
(Glancing back)

643
00:24:04,266 --> 00:24:05,636
You're okay, right?

644
00:24:06,296 --> 00:24:08,465
- No? - What? I'm okay.

645
00:24:08,466 --> 00:24:09,506
- Watch your feet. - Are you okay?

646
00:24:09,936 --> 00:24:11,006
Na Ra, are you okay?

647
00:24:11,206 --> 00:24:13,206
(Instead of answering him, Na Ra only breathes heavily.)

648
00:24:14,046 --> 00:24:17,446
(Even though he's struggling, Na Ra keeps up with them.)

649
00:24:18,276 --> 00:24:21,546
(The momentum builds up from the downhill.)

650
00:24:23,086 --> 00:24:24,186
This is so fun.

651
00:24:24,616 --> 00:24:26,316
- I love it. - He was smiling while running.

652
00:24:27,756 --> 00:24:29,956
- You were also smiling. - I started to have fun.

653
00:24:30,086 --> 00:24:31,895
Only Na Ra isn't smiling.

654
00:24:31,896 --> 00:24:33,326
He's not talking at all.

655
00:24:34,166 --> 00:24:35,925
- At that moment, - Yes.

656
00:24:35,926 --> 00:24:37,535
did you think about the Fun Run?

657
00:24:37,536 --> 00:24:38,995
- Oh, I... - You did, didn't you? Be honest.

658
00:24:38,996 --> 00:24:40,866
- Can I be honest? - You're walking a lot now.

659
00:24:41,336 --> 00:24:43,366
I didn't think about the Fun Run.

660
00:24:43,506 --> 00:24:44,836
- What? - I see.

661
00:24:45,206 --> 00:24:48,745
I just wanted to lock in and focus on the present while running.

662
00:24:48,746 --> 00:24:50,875
- That was my determination. - Right.

663
00:24:50,876 --> 00:24:52,475
Hyun Moo, I get that you're sad.

664
00:24:52,476 --> 00:24:54,115
But don't scowl at him. That's not cool.

665
00:24:54,116 --> 00:24:56,015
- Seriously. - I'm holding myself back.

666
00:24:56,016 --> 00:24:57,855
(Whining)

667
00:24:57,856 --> 00:24:59,156
He's got a soft punch.

668
00:24:59,816 --> 00:25:01,626
(Calm down, Hyun Moo.)

669
00:25:02,026 --> 00:25:04,595
(Na Ra is focused on trail running instead of the Fun Run.)

670
00:25:04,596 --> 00:25:05,955
My gosh. This is only fun...

671
00:25:05,956 --> 00:25:07,326
- because we're running together. - Yes.

672
00:25:07,426 --> 00:25:09,466
Will I be able to do this alone?

673
00:25:10,066 --> 00:25:12,135
- Let's run together. - We can do this together then.

674
00:25:12,136 --> 00:25:13,535
- Great. Thank you. - We can do it together.

675
00:25:13,536 --> 00:25:14,665
- Yes. - Thank you.

676
00:25:14,666 --> 00:25:16,506
Running with other people is much more fun.

677
00:25:16,736 --> 00:25:18,876
Me too. I wanted to run with MINHO. So it's nice to run together today.

678
00:25:19,336 --> 00:25:21,175
You would've given up if you were alone.

679
00:25:21,176 --> 00:25:22,445
- I would've given up. - Right.

680
00:25:22,446 --> 00:25:24,006
No one could do that alone.

681
00:25:25,046 --> 00:25:28,415
(As they run with their members of the crew...)

682
00:25:28,416 --> 00:25:29,586
We're out of the mountain.

683
00:25:30,646 --> 00:25:32,255
(they finally reach their first turning point.)

684
00:25:32,256 --> 00:25:34,686
- This was our first turning point. - My gosh.

685
00:25:34,786 --> 00:25:36,055
No more mountains. Here's an asphalt road.

686
00:25:36,056 --> 00:25:41,596
(Campsite, Turning Point 1, Turning Point 2)

687
00:25:42,066 --> 00:25:44,266
We reached our first turning point.

688
00:25:44,836 --> 00:25:46,495
- And we ran 2.3km. - Hey. I'm wet.

689
00:25:46,496 --> 00:25:48,506
- I'm wet. - We ran for 18 minutes.

690
00:25:48,836 --> 00:25:49,936
- Eighteen minutes? - Yes.

691
00:25:50,136 --> 00:25:51,875
- You ran for 18 minutes? - Yes.

692
00:25:51,876 --> 00:25:53,276
You guys are sweating profusely.

693
00:25:54,946 --> 00:25:56,306
How do you feel now?

694
00:25:56,976 --> 00:25:59,146
When I run 5km, my shirt gets soaked...

695
00:25:59,376 --> 00:26:01,246
- It gets wet like this after 7km. - Don't people do that...

696
00:26:01,686 --> 00:26:02,815
during marathons?

697
00:26:02,816 --> 00:26:05,055
- There are usually water stations. - Right.

698
00:26:05,056 --> 00:26:06,115
There are no water stations...

699
00:26:06,116 --> 00:26:07,215
- during trail running. - You can't get water.

700
00:26:07,216 --> 00:26:08,356
So I brought water.

701
00:26:09,056 --> 00:26:10,955
- It's refreshing. - I have my own routine.

702
00:26:10,956 --> 00:26:11,956
(Out of breath)

703
00:26:12,226 --> 00:26:14,695
We're at our first turning point. I've got something for us.

704
00:26:14,696 --> 00:26:16,466
- Let's fuel up on our energy. - Right.

705
00:26:17,226 --> 00:26:18,395
(He takes something out from his pocket.)

706
00:26:18,396 --> 00:26:20,566
- This is it. I swear. - Okay.

707
00:26:21,306 --> 00:26:22,766
- I take it during HIIT. - What's that?

708
00:26:23,136 --> 00:26:25,075
- It boosts my energy magically. - Really?

709
00:26:25,076 --> 00:26:27,206
I swear. I experienced it myself.

710
00:26:27,236 --> 00:26:30,405
It's mostly carbs.

711
00:26:30,406 --> 00:26:31,875
So you get an energy boost.

712
00:26:31,876 --> 00:26:33,416
This will be super helpful.

713
00:26:33,846 --> 00:26:34,916
Pineapples.

714
00:26:35,786 --> 00:26:37,756
I like pineapple flavors.

715
00:26:38,816 --> 00:26:39,856
- Isn't it good? - Yes.

716
00:26:40,986 --> 00:26:43,586
When I do high-intensity interval training these days,

717
00:26:44,126 --> 00:26:45,625
- I have to take this. - Right.

718
00:26:45,626 --> 00:26:47,526
It boosts my performance too.

719
00:26:48,296 --> 00:26:49,566
We're at our first turning point.

720
00:26:49,966 --> 00:26:51,895
Should we maintain the same pace?

721
00:26:51,896 --> 00:26:53,266
- I'm good. - Sounds good.

722
00:26:53,666 --> 00:26:56,165
Let's boost our energy and keep running.

723
00:26:56,166 --> 00:26:57,775
- We got this. - I can put them back in here.

724
00:26:57,776 --> 00:26:59,776
(He puts away the wrappers in his pocket.)

725
00:27:00,436 --> 00:27:01,746
- Let's go. - Let's go.

726
00:27:02,076 --> 00:27:03,146
Let's go.

727
00:27:03,276 --> 00:27:06,446
(Running wearily)

728
00:27:07,616 --> 00:27:09,386
Wait, there it is. It's his signature form.

729
00:27:10,786 --> 00:27:13,016
(He takes this running form whenever he's exhausted.)

730
00:27:14,116 --> 00:27:15,556
Let's go!

731
00:27:16,126 --> 00:27:17,325
- Gosh. - We got this.

732
00:27:17,326 --> 00:27:18,456
We got this.

733
00:27:18,926 --> 00:27:20,155
(The Proper Run Crew goes back into the mountain.)

734
00:27:20,156 --> 00:27:21,996
My thighs are killing me after the break.

735
00:27:23,226 --> 00:27:24,435
My gosh, they're killing me.

736
00:27:24,436 --> 00:27:26,896
(Campsite, Turning Point 1, Turning Point 2)

737
00:27:27,566 --> 00:27:31,676
(Their energy is fully charged.)

738
00:27:33,036 --> 00:27:34,846
- Let's do 3km. - Let's do 3km.

739
00:27:35,476 --> 00:27:37,006
- Let's do 7 minutes and 30 seconds. - Okay.

740
00:27:38,716 --> 00:27:42,316
(They pick up the pace after the break.)

741
00:27:44,786 --> 00:27:46,585
- He was no joke. He was barefoot. - Barefoot?

742
00:27:46,586 --> 00:27:47,686
- What? - Gosh.

743
00:27:49,156 --> 00:27:50,626
- He's running barefoot? - My gosh.

744
00:27:50,926 --> 00:27:52,396
That's Kian84 when he gets older.

745
00:27:53,356 --> 00:27:55,966
- He might be doing just that. - He's Kian84's future.

746
00:27:58,236 --> 00:28:00,535
(As they run past the barefooted pro,)

747
00:28:00,536 --> 00:28:03,066
(they focus on trail running again.)

748
00:28:05,476 --> 00:28:11,216
(Repeatedly going uphill and downhill)

749
00:28:13,016 --> 00:28:14,016
Gosh, the stairs.

750
00:28:14,246 --> 00:28:15,785
- Darn it. - Let's do this.

751
00:28:15,786 --> 00:28:19,086
(Na Ra is tired and ends up walking.)

752
00:28:19,756 --> 00:28:21,656
- Let's slow down on the stairs. - Yes.

753
00:28:24,326 --> 00:28:27,356
(But MINHO is doing fine.)

754
00:28:27,866 --> 00:28:31,066
(Panting)

755
00:28:32,036 --> 00:28:34,506
Gosh, MINHO's breathing was so stable.

756
00:28:35,566 --> 00:28:38,306
(On the other hand, the older members are drained.)

757
00:28:38,876 --> 00:28:41,006
- Kian84. Why do trail running? - Yes?

758
00:28:41,806 --> 00:28:42,806
Trail running?

759
00:28:43,146 --> 00:28:45,776
Trail running makes road running...

760
00:28:46,276 --> 00:28:47,685
- much easier. - Really?

761
00:28:47,686 --> 00:28:48,716
Yes.

762
00:28:50,616 --> 00:28:54,216
(The crew chief resumes running after encouraging him.)

763
00:28:54,356 --> 00:28:57,086
(Na Ra follow the crew chief and runs again.)

764
00:28:59,426 --> 00:29:02,766
If we keep walking, we'll lose our rhythm.

765
00:29:04,836 --> 00:29:06,465
- Na Ra, you're okay. Right? - I'm okay.

766
00:29:06,466 --> 00:29:07,966
- Okay. - I'm not okay.

767
00:29:08,166 --> 00:29:09,266
- Okay. - Okay.

768
00:29:11,736 --> 00:29:14,236
Wait. Na Ra is exhausted.

769
00:29:15,176 --> 00:29:18,376
(Na Ra keeps on trying and catches up with them.)

770
00:29:20,276 --> 00:29:21,785
Don't tense up your thighs. Focus on your toes.

771
00:29:21,786 --> 00:29:22,786
- Toes. - Engage your toes.

772
00:29:22,787 --> 00:29:23,816
- Toes. - Yes.

773
00:29:26,286 --> 00:29:29,686
(He starts running and stops soon afterward.)

774
00:29:30,996 --> 00:29:32,525
Na Ra was the ace member...

775
00:29:32,526 --> 00:29:33,955
- during the Fun Run. - I know.

776
00:29:33,956 --> 00:29:36,065
He ran while smiling like a carp.

777
00:29:36,066 --> 00:29:37,465
- He was the winner among us. - That's right.

778
00:29:37,466 --> 00:29:38,735
Things are different now.

779
00:29:38,736 --> 00:29:40,736
What's the point of doing something that doesn't make us smile?

780
00:29:42,566 --> 00:29:46,236
I think it was when we were past 2km.

781
00:29:46,936 --> 00:29:50,546
My vision turned blurry,

782
00:29:51,646 --> 00:29:55,416
and my body became slow.

783
00:29:56,086 --> 00:29:58,015
The weather was hot, my body was sweaty,

784
00:29:58,016 --> 00:29:59,285
- my legs hurt, - That's right.

785
00:29:59,286 --> 00:30:00,415
and I was out of breath.

786
00:30:00,416 --> 00:30:02,226
You weren't used to running in the mountains.

787
00:30:02,886 --> 00:30:05,526
My body and mind weren't in sync.

788
00:30:05,896 --> 00:30:09,026
It was so exhausting, and my vision was blurry.

789
00:30:09,696 --> 00:30:11,266
You should've had bread during the run.

790
00:30:11,636 --> 00:30:13,995
- You should've had bread. - You didn't go to a supermarket.

791
00:30:13,996 --> 00:30:15,036
- That's right. - Was that the reason?

792
00:30:16,106 --> 00:30:19,376
(You should have carbs during a run.)

793
00:30:21,076 --> 00:30:24,175
(It'll clear up your vision.)

794
00:30:24,176 --> 00:30:27,885
You were good during the Fun Run because you ate bread.

795
00:30:27,886 --> 00:30:29,116
(There was a reason why we did that during the Fun Run, okay?)

796
00:30:30,186 --> 00:30:31,556
Na Ra, are you okay?

797
00:30:32,256 --> 00:30:33,356
- What? - Are you okay?

798
00:30:33,516 --> 00:30:34,586
Who are you?

799
00:30:35,126 --> 00:30:36,786
Who... Who are you?

800
00:30:37,326 --> 00:30:38,425
- Na Ra. - Yes?

801
00:30:38,426 --> 00:30:40,356
- Relax your shoulders. - Relax my shoulders?

802
00:30:40,526 --> 00:30:41,866
- Relax your shoulders. - Okay.

803
00:30:41,966 --> 00:30:43,426
- My shoulders feel tight. - Relax your shoulders...

804
00:30:43,726 --> 00:30:45,766
- and tighten up your nose. - Good.

805
00:30:46,666 --> 00:30:49,735
He led me with a sense of responsibility.

806
00:30:49,736 --> 00:30:50,966
- I was so thankful. - You'll breathe more easily.

807
00:30:51,276 --> 00:30:53,376
It's important to have someone who cheers you on by your side.

808
00:30:54,336 --> 00:30:56,545
All of us run well. This is incredible.

809
00:30:56,546 --> 00:30:58,046
(Kian84 and MINHO look trustworthy in front of Na Ra.)

810
00:31:00,316 --> 00:31:01,985
Okay. Our pace is 7 minutes and 40 seconds per km.

811
00:31:01,986 --> 00:31:03,115
- Okay. - We kept up with the pace.

812
00:31:03,116 --> 00:31:04,146
Nice.

813
00:31:04,786 --> 00:31:06,886
- They've run at that pace for 4km. - They're fast.

814
00:31:08,486 --> 00:31:09,926
Our pace is really good right now.

815
00:31:10,286 --> 00:31:11,725
We might enter the six-minute range at this rate.

816
00:31:11,726 --> 00:31:12,755
- Really? - Yes.

817
00:31:12,756 --> 00:31:13,756
In the mountains...

818
00:31:15,196 --> 00:31:17,396
We did it! We're at 5km, and the pace is 6 minutes and 46 seconds.

819
00:31:17,496 --> 00:31:18,836
- Six minutes and forty-six seconds. - This is insane.

820
00:31:19,866 --> 00:31:21,166
We're good at setting the pace.

821
00:31:21,536 --> 00:31:22,536
Nice.

822
00:31:23,406 --> 00:31:25,035
I think both of you run very well.

823
00:31:25,036 --> 00:31:26,176
I think we can go more slowly.

824
00:31:26,536 --> 00:31:27,536
Hey.

825
00:31:27,537 --> 00:31:29,476
- We should keep up with the pace. - "I think we can go more slowly."

826
00:31:30,546 --> 00:31:31,546
(That didn't work.)

827
00:31:31,547 --> 00:31:33,646
Your body becomes more tired when you walk.

828
00:31:35,616 --> 00:31:38,486
(They gather up their strength and keep up with the pace.)

829
00:31:39,086 --> 00:31:40,315
This is Turning Point Two.

830
00:31:40,316 --> 00:31:41,855
(They arrive at Turing Point 2.)

831
00:31:41,856 --> 00:31:43,385
(Exhausted)

832
00:31:43,386 --> 00:31:44,995
How many kilometers have you run?

833
00:31:44,996 --> 00:31:46,326
Over 5km.

834
00:31:46,426 --> 00:31:47,456
Turning Point Two.

835
00:31:47,866 --> 00:31:49,826
Shall we have a short break?

836
00:31:51,096 --> 00:31:52,396
We have a bit of water left.

837
00:31:54,136 --> 00:31:55,805
- It felt like a dream. - Drink first.

838
00:31:55,806 --> 00:31:57,436
- No, drink first. - Thank you.

839
00:31:58,176 --> 00:32:01,036
(He gives water to Na Ra since he is struggling the most.)

840
00:32:01,406 --> 00:32:03,146
- MINHO, did you drink water? - I'm okay, Kian84.

841
00:32:04,716 --> 00:32:07,346
(He drinks water after looking after the crew members.)

842
00:32:08,146 --> 00:32:09,485
My facial expression is bad.

843
00:32:09,486 --> 00:32:10,515
It's bad.

844
00:32:10,516 --> 00:32:13,115
You should've just eaten rice or glass noodles...

845
00:32:13,116 --> 00:32:14,386
at my place.

846
00:32:16,226 --> 00:32:18,596
(Taking out)

847
00:32:19,156 --> 00:32:20,526
- It's wet, but... - It's okay.

848
00:32:20,696 --> 00:32:21,766
What is it?

849
00:32:22,666 --> 00:32:24,466
- Really? - Right. He needs red bean jelly.

850
00:32:25,466 --> 00:32:26,466
Thanks.

851
00:32:26,467 --> 00:32:28,666
I was moved at that moment.

852
00:32:29,636 --> 00:32:31,435
You need to eat to keep going.

853
00:32:31,436 --> 00:32:32,775
(The crew chief has a sweet treat thanks to MINHO.)

854
00:32:32,776 --> 00:32:35,276
(Chewing)

855
00:32:36,076 --> 00:32:38,816
(He takes a bite after taking care of the older members.)

856
00:32:39,316 --> 00:32:40,876
- Let's go. Let's set off. - Okay.

857
00:32:41,076 --> 00:32:42,286
- Let's go! - Okay, let's do this!

858
00:32:42,346 --> 00:32:43,746
- Let's go. Let's do this. - Okay.

859
00:32:44,516 --> 00:32:46,185
- Let's go. - Let's go.

860
00:32:46,186 --> 00:32:47,655
(They set off for the campsite.)

861
00:32:47,656 --> 00:32:49,686
- The next section is 1.5km long. - Will they start running again?

862
00:32:50,526 --> 00:32:53,696
I bet I had lost about 1.5kg.

863
00:32:54,156 --> 00:32:55,525
- I know. - I bet I had lost all the water.

864
00:32:55,526 --> 00:32:56,796
(That's incredible.)

865
00:32:58,336 --> 00:32:59,765
- MINHO, be the pacemaker. - Okay.

866
00:32:59,766 --> 00:33:00,996
- Shall I lead? - Yes.

867
00:33:01,306 --> 00:33:02,306
He is cool.

868
00:33:02,307 --> 00:33:03,706
(Speeding up)

869
00:33:03,866 --> 00:33:06,436
MINHO moved to the front and back...

870
00:33:06,636 --> 00:33:08,175
- to push us. - He pushed us from the back...

871
00:33:08,176 --> 00:33:09,646
- Yes. - and pulled us from the front.

872
00:33:10,876 --> 00:33:12,316
It's hard to run after a break.

873
00:33:12,616 --> 00:33:14,516
Right? It's like that.

874
00:33:15,046 --> 00:33:16,215
- Is it the same for you? - It's hard at first...

875
00:33:16,216 --> 00:33:17,346
if you resume running after a break.

876
00:33:18,186 --> 00:33:19,886
It takes a while to get used to the pace again.

877
00:33:20,486 --> 00:33:22,025
Since it's steep, we'll run slowly.

878
00:33:22,026 --> 00:33:23,026
Slowly.

879
00:33:23,386 --> 00:33:24,655
Let's take small steps to go up.

880
00:33:24,656 --> 00:33:27,326
Our pacemaker is very good.

881
00:33:27,426 --> 00:33:28,826
- Seriously. - He is amazing.

882
00:33:30,126 --> 00:33:33,236
Let's take small steps instead of stopping.

883
00:33:34,666 --> 00:33:36,165
- You have to use your glutes here. - Glutes.

884
00:33:36,166 --> 00:33:37,205
Use your glutes.

885
00:33:37,206 --> 00:33:38,475
(MINHO leads the older members while coaching them constantly.)

886
00:33:38,476 --> 00:33:40,606
- Small steps. - Small steps.

887
00:33:41,276 --> 00:33:43,405
- Small steps. Glutes. - Use your glutes.

888
00:33:43,406 --> 00:33:44,446
This way.

889
00:33:45,716 --> 00:33:48,016
If you keep walking, your legs will give out.

890
00:33:48,386 --> 00:33:49,585
- Don't do that. - Okay.

891
00:33:49,586 --> 00:33:50,615
All right.

892
00:33:50,616 --> 00:33:52,315
(With MINHO's encouragement)

893
00:33:52,316 --> 00:33:53,615
- Okay. We're at 6km. - Okay.

894
00:33:53,616 --> 00:33:54,656
The pace is 8 minutes and 44 seconds.

895
00:33:56,586 --> 00:34:00,296
(Na Ra follows them well with small steps.)

896
00:34:00,426 --> 00:34:01,595
Your legs aren't too tired, right? It was okay, right?

897
00:34:01,596 --> 00:34:02,596
- It was okay. - Yes.

898
00:34:02,597 --> 00:34:03,866
- It was much better than before. - Yes.

899
00:34:04,126 --> 00:34:05,235
- Let's go. - Let's go.

900
00:34:05,236 --> 00:34:06,265
- The best runner... - Let's go.

901
00:34:06,266 --> 00:34:07,965
- needs to be at the front. - That's right.

902
00:34:07,966 --> 00:34:09,866
- Then it's easy to follow him. - I agree.

903
00:34:10,836 --> 00:34:12,605
Watch the stairs. Let's take small steps.

904
00:34:12,606 --> 00:34:13,706
- Small steps. - No big steps.

905
00:34:14,646 --> 00:34:17,046
(They take small steps for the stairs as well.)

906
00:34:17,776 --> 00:34:20,075
(Why is Na Ra taking big steps?)

907
00:34:20,076 --> 00:34:22,745
- I had no strength in my legs. - I see.

908
00:34:22,746 --> 00:34:23,816
His strength is gone.

909
00:34:24,086 --> 00:34:25,855
This way, your feet won't get tired.

910
00:34:25,856 --> 00:34:28,985
I think Na Ra's skin tone looks weird.

911
00:34:28,986 --> 00:34:30,185
- I know. - It's ashen.

912
00:34:30,186 --> 00:34:31,996
He looks like a ghost on MINHO's shoulder.

913
00:34:32,826 --> 00:34:34,196
That's scary. Stop it.

914
00:34:35,026 --> 00:34:36,125
(Glancing over)

915
00:34:36,126 --> 00:34:37,326
Na Ra, your steps are too big.

916
00:34:37,496 --> 00:34:38,996
- I... - You're taking strides.

917
00:34:39,196 --> 00:34:40,795
- If I take small steps, - Small steps.

918
00:34:40,796 --> 00:34:42,406
my hip joints hurt.

919
00:34:43,166 --> 00:34:44,405
My hip joints hurt.

920
00:34:44,406 --> 00:34:46,405
- How do they hurt? - They get pinched.

921
00:34:46,406 --> 00:34:47,576
- They get pinched. - Yes.

922
00:34:47,946 --> 00:34:49,376
- Do they get pinched? - They get pinched.

923
00:34:49,976 --> 00:34:51,416
So I keep taking big steps.

924
00:34:51,516 --> 00:34:52,815
It'll be very exhausting to take big steps.

925
00:34:52,816 --> 00:34:53,946
If I take big steps...

926
00:34:54,646 --> 00:34:57,446
like you and MINHO say, I get tired right away.

927
00:34:58,756 --> 00:35:01,355
Na Ra, let's go at your pace for the last section.

928
00:35:01,356 --> 00:35:04,626
(Na Ra, let's go at your pace for the last section.)

929
00:35:05,456 --> 00:35:06,725
- Na Ra, - Yes?

930
00:35:06,726 --> 00:35:09,296
go at the pace that feels comfortable to you.

931
00:35:09,366 --> 00:35:10,696
We'll follow you.

932
00:35:12,936 --> 00:35:15,905
(But his stamina reaches its limits.)

933
00:35:15,906 --> 00:35:17,105
He is walking.

934
00:35:17,106 --> 00:35:19,106
- Take the lead. - Hurry up and run.

935
00:35:19,336 --> 00:35:20,805
My heart rate is 188bpm.

936
00:35:20,806 --> 00:35:22,545
- MINHO, set the pace. - Is his heart rate 188bpm?

937
00:35:22,546 --> 00:35:24,005
- MINHO, go ahead. - MINHO, be the pacemaker.

938
00:35:24,006 --> 00:35:25,015
Okay.

939
00:35:25,016 --> 00:35:26,775
(In the end, MINHO becomes the pacemaker again.)

940
00:35:26,776 --> 00:35:28,416
- MINHO and Kian84 are incredible. - Let's go.

941
00:35:29,986 --> 00:35:31,316
How are they so athletic?

942
00:35:32,456 --> 00:35:33,556
It was a crisis.

943
00:35:34,556 --> 00:35:36,486
I had one crisis after another.

944
00:35:37,756 --> 00:35:40,426
"I want to run well. But I won't be able to run well."

945
00:35:40,556 --> 00:35:41,726
"No, I'll run well."

946
00:35:42,396 --> 00:35:44,666
"But I won't be able to run well." I had those thoughts...

947
00:35:45,266 --> 00:35:47,036
over and over again.

948
00:35:48,766 --> 00:35:52,806
(He follows them as if his life depends on it.)

949
00:35:55,006 --> 00:35:57,676
(Grabbing)

950
00:35:59,676 --> 00:36:02,985
(Will Na Ra get a helping hand?)

951
00:36:02,986 --> 00:36:04,016
Hold on a second.

952
00:36:05,247 --> 00:36:09,417
(He follows them as if his life depends on it.)

953
00:36:11,587 --> 00:36:14,257
(Grabbing)

954
00:36:15,757 --> 00:36:16,826
(The crew chief holds his wrist.)

955
00:36:16,827 --> 00:36:17,857
Hold on a second.

956
00:36:20,727 --> 00:36:22,596
(Na Ra, you can do it.)

957
00:36:22,597 --> 00:36:24,466
I didn't know there was such a heartfelt moment.

958
00:36:24,467 --> 00:36:25,496
(Praising himself)

959
00:36:25,497 --> 00:36:26,497
Seriously.

960
00:36:26,498 --> 00:36:28,736
It was one spoonful and gratitude...

961
00:36:28,737 --> 00:36:30,536
and the thought, "Please let go of me."

962
00:36:30,537 --> 00:36:34,807
(Please let go of me.)

963
00:36:35,277 --> 00:36:36,446
(Chuckling)

964
00:36:36,447 --> 00:36:38,046
- "Stop!" - Ten spoonfuls of that.

965
00:36:38,047 --> 00:36:39,147
"Stop!"

966
00:36:39,477 --> 00:36:40,917
- "Please let go of me." - I was too exhausted.

967
00:36:41,717 --> 00:36:42,817
We're nearly there.

968
00:36:44,657 --> 00:36:45,717
We're nearly there.

969
00:36:46,487 --> 00:36:47,926
We were nearly at the end.

970
00:36:47,927 --> 00:36:49,086
- I know. - Walking at the end...

971
00:36:49,087 --> 00:36:50,286
would've made him regretful.

972
00:36:50,287 --> 00:36:52,126
- That's right. - So I encouraged him...

973
00:36:52,127 --> 00:36:54,056
- to run until the end. - My goodness.

974
00:36:54,057 --> 00:36:55,267
(He pushes Na Ra from the back until the very end.)

975
00:36:55,667 --> 00:36:57,996
- We're nearly there. - Let's cheer up.

976
00:36:57,997 --> 00:36:59,397
(They're close to the campsite now.)

977
00:37:00,097 --> 00:37:01,237
Keep following me.

978
00:37:04,167 --> 00:37:05,837
(Exhausted)

979
00:37:06,537 --> 00:37:07,737
Kian84, be the pacemaker.

980
00:37:08,147 --> 00:37:09,147
- All right. - Okay.

981
00:37:09,148 --> 00:37:10,876
- Let's stay close together. - We keep going faster.

982
00:37:10,877 --> 00:37:12,117
No, we aren't going fast.

983
00:37:13,947 --> 00:37:16,587
(All right. Let's do this.)

984
00:37:17,187 --> 00:37:18,456
(I did 2 people's worth in the Fun Run Crew.)

985
00:37:18,457 --> 00:37:20,287
He was a completely different person.

986
00:37:20,457 --> 00:37:22,626
You belong in the Fun Run Crew.

987
00:37:22,627 --> 00:37:24,226
You're the ace member in the Fun Run Crew.

988
00:37:24,227 --> 00:37:25,357
You're the ace member.

989
00:37:25,527 --> 00:37:27,226
- Be the head of a snake. - Be the head of a snake,

990
00:37:27,227 --> 00:37:28,726
not the tail of a dragon.

991
00:37:28,727 --> 00:37:30,496
The head of a snake is better than the tail of a dragon.

992
00:37:30,497 --> 00:37:32,597
- The head of a snake is better. - That's right.

993
00:37:34,767 --> 00:37:36,707
- You can do it. - All right.

994
00:37:37,607 --> 00:37:40,537
(Someone save the tail.)

995
00:37:41,007 --> 00:37:43,047
I always have this thought when things get hard at the end.

996
00:37:43,607 --> 00:37:45,077
"To do this,"

997
00:37:45,277 --> 00:37:46,717
"I endured all those hardships."

998
00:37:47,047 --> 00:37:50,617
I still keep those words close to my heart.

999
00:37:50,887 --> 00:37:52,757
How cool. They're like special forces.

1000
00:37:53,117 --> 00:37:54,487
This is the moment you get a workout.

1001
00:37:56,227 --> 00:37:57,356
This way.

1002
00:37:57,357 --> 00:37:59,456
(They've braved strong winds...)

1003
00:37:59,457 --> 00:38:02,766
(and rough waves.)

1004
00:38:02,767 --> 00:38:05,037
We're nearly there. I see the starting point.

1005
00:38:05,097 --> 00:38:06,596
- Let's run at full speed. - Okay.

1006
00:38:06,597 --> 00:38:08,236
- Let's run. - Let's go.

1007
00:38:08,237 --> 00:38:10,567
- Run at full speed? - Let's go.

1008
00:38:11,396 --> 00:38:12,905
(Every member...)

1009
00:38:12,906 --> 00:38:15,776
(of the crew...)

1010
00:38:17,436 --> 00:38:21,306
(runs at full speed toward the finish line.)

1011
00:38:23,676 --> 00:38:25,785
(They pass the finish line as one.)

1012
00:38:25,786 --> 00:38:26,846
Na Ra.

1013
00:38:27,616 --> 00:38:29,616
(We did it.)

1014
00:38:30,756 --> 00:38:32,985
(They succeed in completing about 8km of trail running.)

1015
00:38:32,986 --> 00:38:34,885
We did it. Let's walk.

1016
00:38:34,886 --> 00:38:36,825
Watching this after the Fun Run...

1017
00:38:36,826 --> 00:38:38,526
really makes me see the difference.

1018
00:38:39,496 --> 00:38:41,936
Right? There is a big difference.

1019
00:38:42,036 --> 00:38:45,066
- We thought we were cool. - "This isn't it."

1020
00:38:45,306 --> 00:38:46,536
You were cool, Ji Hyeon.

1021
00:38:46,806 --> 00:38:48,275
We were cool.

1022
00:38:48,276 --> 00:38:50,335
- You won't get that taste. - You really won't.

1023
00:38:50,336 --> 00:38:51,336
(Triumphant)

1024
00:38:52,676 --> 00:38:54,146
- You ran really well. - We did 8km of trail running.

1025
00:38:54,676 --> 00:38:56,846
It's my first time doing such a thing without a break.

1026
00:38:57,316 --> 00:38:59,785
Usually, my legs give out when I reach the finish line.

1027
00:38:59,786 --> 00:39:00,916
But this is...

1028
00:39:01,116 --> 00:39:02,985
- Both are hard, but it's better. - You have strength in your legs.

1029
00:39:02,986 --> 00:39:05,286
- It's a bit better. - Yes. Both are hard. Exactly.

1030
00:39:05,426 --> 00:39:06,956
- But your legs get less tired. - It's a bit better.

1031
00:39:07,056 --> 00:39:08,156
I see.

1032
00:39:08,256 --> 00:39:09,996
- My goodness. Hold on. - Still...

1033
