But he slowed down for us. I'm grateful for that.

1281
00:48:02,896 --> 00:48:03,896
(He is thankful that MINHO ran with them.)

1282
00:48:03,897 --> 00:48:07,065
As for Na Ra, the pace was much faster...

1283
00:48:07,066 --> 00:48:08,626
than his usual one.

1284
00:48:08,866 --> 00:48:11,436
But he kept up until the end. I'm grateful for that.

1285
00:48:11,996 --> 00:48:15,836
I'm grateful for both of them.

1286
00:48:16,636 --> 00:48:17,706
Yes.

1287
00:48:18,476 --> 00:48:20,506
Would it have been possible for Moo Do Ra Ji?

1288
00:48:23,776 --> 00:48:25,985
- Come on! - Let me explain.

1289
00:48:25,986 --> 00:48:27,546
- Gosh! - Na Ra!

1290
00:48:27,716 --> 00:48:29,155
- Na Ra... - Gosh!

1291
00:48:29,156 --> 00:48:30,615
says unnecessary things.

1292
00:48:30,616 --> 00:48:31,785
- Right. - Na Ra!

1293
00:48:31,786 --> 00:48:33,926
- He opened a can of worms. - He asks for trouble.

1294
00:48:34,126 --> 00:48:36,356
I should find two more people when he leaves.

1295
00:48:36,456 --> 00:48:37,596
- Sunmoo! - Sunmoo?

1296
00:48:37,996 --> 00:48:39,525
- Uphill! - Uphill!

1297
00:48:39,526 --> 00:48:42,536
(The Fun Run is open to any kind.)

1298
00:48:43,066 --> 00:48:44,335
He's the fastest one around me.

1299
00:48:44,336 --> 00:48:45,866
(Future Fun Run ace, Sunmoo?)

1300
00:48:47,306 --> 00:48:49,606
Sit here. Your legs shouldn't stiffen up.

1301
00:48:50,606 --> 00:48:51,975
(Faltering)

1302
00:48:51,976 --> 00:48:53,476
Sit on a higher place.

1303
00:48:54,306 --> 00:48:57,346
(They arrive at the campsite while sweating buckets.)

1304
00:48:57,576 --> 00:48:59,216
- Run in the mountains? - Look at my sweat.

1305
00:48:59,846 --> 00:49:01,016
He's sweating a lot.

1306
00:49:01,716 --> 00:49:03,716
Even your sweat looks nice.

1307
00:49:03,916 --> 00:49:06,686
Right. Even your sweat looks nice.

1308
00:49:07,356 --> 00:49:09,425
The shape of the sweat looks rounder than others.

1309
00:49:09,426 --> 00:49:10,656
Did you use a spray?

1310
00:49:10,926 --> 00:49:11,926
The shape is...

1311
00:49:12,496 --> 00:49:14,225
The shape looks nice and round.

1312
00:49:14,226 --> 00:49:15,226
(Even the sweat of the ace shines.)

1313
00:49:15,526 --> 00:49:17,696
But keep this in mind. I'm the leader.

1314
00:49:17,996 --> 00:49:19,206
Of course.

1315
00:49:19,906 --> 00:49:21,005
- Kian84! - Well...

1316
00:49:21,006 --> 00:49:23,475
Why think that? I came here because of you.

1317
00:49:23,476 --> 00:49:26,505
Actually, MINHO led all of us.

1318
00:49:26,506 --> 00:49:29,145
- We did follow your pace. - Right.

1319
00:49:29,146 --> 00:49:30,975
Even though I may be a figurehead, I'm the leader.

1320
00:49:30,976 --> 00:49:32,715
- Of course, I know that. - You're the leader.

1321
00:49:32,716 --> 00:49:33,985
- I'm... - The enforcer?

1322
00:49:33,986 --> 00:49:35,885
- No. I'm the training director. - Training director.

1323
00:49:35,886 --> 00:49:37,885
- In crews, - The training director?

1324
00:49:37,886 --> 00:49:39,785
there are training directors.

1325
00:49:39,786 --> 00:49:41,785
I'll be the one to come up with the courses...

1326
00:49:41,786 --> 00:49:43,595
- Right. - and be the pacemaker.

1327
00:49:43,596 --> 00:49:44,795
Those people are the big shots.

1328
00:49:44,796 --> 00:49:45,995
- The training director. - Right.

1329
00:49:45,996 --> 00:49:47,125
I'll be the cooking director.

1330
00:49:47,126 --> 00:49:48,666
The cooking director? All right.

1331
00:49:48,796 --> 00:49:50,696
- I'll always bring ice and drinks. - Right.

1332
00:49:51,236 --> 00:49:52,705
- You're the crew leader. - Right.

1333
00:49:52,706 --> 00:49:53,766
I'm the training director.

1334
00:49:54,006 --> 00:49:55,435
- You're the cooking director. - Cooking director.

1335
00:49:55,436 --> 00:49:57,405
- That's great. - We must all have a title.

1336
00:49:57,406 --> 00:49:58,976
(They have even distributed their roles.)

1337
00:49:59,846 --> 00:50:01,375
Should we wash up first?

1338
00:50:01,376 --> 00:50:03,246
- Right. Let's wash up. - We've sweated a lot.

1339
00:50:03,716 --> 00:50:05,375
- Let's wash up. - Is there a place we can wash up?

1340
00:50:05,376 --> 00:50:06,916
- Over there. - They have showers.

1341
00:50:07,316 --> 00:50:08,985
- Let's go! - Let's go.

1342
00:50:08,986 --> 00:50:10,516
(They move to wash away their sweat.)

1343
00:50:12,556 --> 00:50:14,755
(They even take showers together...)

1344
00:50:14,756 --> 00:50:20,196
(in the Proper Run Crew.)

1345
00:50:20,296 --> 00:50:21,866
I saw everything.

1346
00:50:23,566 --> 00:50:24,736
Na Ra...

1347
00:50:25,666 --> 00:50:26,736
and MINHO's...

1348
00:50:27,836 --> 00:50:28,936
everything.

1349
00:50:29,476 --> 00:50:30,875
(Wriggling)

1350
00:50:30,876 --> 00:50:32,876
(What did Kian84 see?)

1351
00:50:33,642 --> 00:50:35,142
I saw everything.

1352
00:50:36,042 --> 00:50:37,142
Na Ra...

1353
00:50:37,812 --> 00:50:38,942
and MINHO's...

1354
00:50:40,512 --> 00:50:42,811
everything.

1355
00:50:42,812 --> 00:50:45,151
(I saw everything.)

1356
00:50:45,152 --> 00:50:46,351
- Kian84! - What was that?

1357
00:50:46,352 --> 00:50:48,092
(Shocked)

1358
00:50:48,452 --> 00:50:49,651
What was that?

1359
00:50:49,652 --> 00:50:51,421
- Gosh. - What's wrong with your eyes?

1360
00:50:51,422 --> 00:50:53,191
That day, I was a bit...

1361
00:50:53,192 --> 00:50:54,831
- Why did you bring your eyebrow up? - I was a bit drunk.

1362
00:50:54,832 --> 00:50:56,791
This can become a reason for leaving the crew.

1363
00:50:56,792 --> 00:50:59,331
- Don't get the wrong idea. - "Don't get the wrong idea."

1364
00:50:59,332 --> 00:51:00,562
That's so disgusting.

1365
00:51:00,632 --> 00:51:02,971
The showers had no screens.

1366
00:51:02,972 --> 00:51:05,241
- Right. - That's how men wash up together.

1367
00:51:05,242 --> 00:51:06,741
- Right. - It felt like being in the army.

1368
00:51:06,742 --> 00:51:08,211
Well, that's fine.

1369
00:51:08,212 --> 00:51:09,811
It's just his eyes.

1370
00:51:09,812 --> 00:51:11,942
He brought his eyebrow up.

1371
00:51:13,282 --> 00:51:15,182
They all looked great.

1372
00:51:15,552 --> 00:51:17,552
They were healthy young men.

1373
00:51:17,982 --> 00:51:19,682
As an athlete,

1374
00:51:19,782 --> 00:51:21,892
it was inevitable for me...

1375
00:51:22,952 --> 00:51:25,292
to check out their body lines.

1376
00:51:25,492 --> 00:51:29,832
I checked how fit their bodies were.

1377
00:51:29,992 --> 00:51:32,531
We got a lot closer after running and taking a shower together.

1378
00:51:32,532 --> 00:51:34,701
(The crew members got a lot closer.)

1379
00:51:34,702 --> 00:51:36,832
That was great. That was a refreshing shower.

1380
00:51:38,272 --> 00:51:39,501
Are we going to eat?

1381
00:51:39,502 --> 00:51:41,102
- We should eat. - I'm so hungry.

1382
00:51:43,012 --> 00:51:44,071
(I Live Alone)

1383
00:51:44,072 --> 00:51:45,141
(Filial Piety Scenario)

1384
00:51:45,142 --> 00:51:46,442
- "Scenario." - "Filial Piety?"

1385
00:51:48,882 --> 00:51:50,152
- What? - Is that his mother's house?

1386
00:51:50,252 --> 00:51:51,411
- It's Ju Seung. - It's his mother's house.

1387
00:51:51,412 --> 00:51:52,581
(Ju Seung is doing something at his mother's house.)

1388
00:51:52,582 --> 00:51:53,752
(Busy)

1389
00:51:54,622 --> 00:51:55,652
What are you doing?

1390
00:51:58,692 --> 00:51:59,762
So...

1391
00:52:00,662 --> 00:52:01,692
- Gosh! - What is that?

1392
00:52:01,862 --> 00:52:05,261
I don't think the aged kimchi is ready.

1393
00:52:05,262 --> 00:52:06,361
It tastes amazing when you stir-fry aged kimchi.

1394
00:52:06,362 --> 00:52:08,531
- His mother is a great cook. - Right.

1395
00:52:08,532 --> 00:52:09,571
Right.

1396
00:52:09,572 --> 00:52:11,201
I'll add this as well.

1397
00:52:11,202 --> 00:52:13,172
(I should get back to work.)

1398
00:52:14,142 --> 00:52:16,341
(He hurriedly...)

1399
00:52:16,342 --> 00:52:19,642
(starts preparing the tomatoes.)

1400
00:52:20,282 --> 00:52:21,442
Get some cold water first.

1401
00:52:21,752 --> 00:52:25,582
I'll be visiting an important person with my mom today.

1402
00:52:25,882 --> 00:52:28,552
I came to my mother's house to get things prepared.

1403
00:52:28,722 --> 00:52:29,992
Ju Seung must be cooking.

1404
00:52:31,662 --> 00:52:34,392
Which country eats a lot of tomatoes?

1405
00:52:35,032 --> 00:52:36,032
Italy.

1406
00:52:37,162 --> 00:52:38,232
Spaghetti.

1407
00:52:38,962 --> 00:52:41,501
- It prevents cancer. - He's into something again.

1408
00:52:41,502 --> 00:52:43,471
He's been saying that to me for months.

1409
00:52:43,472 --> 00:52:45,542
- Tomatoes? - As for tomatoes,

1410
00:52:46,072 --> 00:52:48,342
they help with your immune system and build anticancer activities.

1411
00:52:48,672 --> 00:52:51,582
They are great in many different aspects.

1412
00:52:51,882 --> 00:52:53,982
I felt a lot of change.

1413
00:52:54,312 --> 00:52:56,251
- I started drinking tomato juice. - Why am I in outer space?

1414
00:52:56,252 --> 00:52:58,111
Why is the background always like that for you?

1415
00:52:58,112 --> 00:52:59,181
I was being serious!

1416
00:52:59,182 --> 00:53:00,252
That seems like...

1417
00:53:00,722 --> 00:53:01,892
(Feeling wronged)

1418
00:53:01,952 --> 00:53:03,651
I'm planning to give this important person...

1419
00:53:03,652 --> 00:53:05,322
some tomato juice.

1420
00:53:06,022 --> 00:53:07,321
- Tomato juice? - Right.

1421
00:53:07,322 --> 00:53:09,392
- Tomato juice? - I drink it every day.

1422
00:53:09,562 --> 00:53:10,761
I drink around 700ml every day.

1423
00:53:10,762 --> 00:53:12,302
Hasn't it been a year since you started?

1424
00:53:12,402 --> 00:53:14,001
It hasn't been that long. It has been around half a year.

1425
00:53:14,002 --> 00:53:16,271
I'm serious about this. Even with a little bit of sleep,

1426
00:53:16,272 --> 00:53:18,001
it feels like I slept for a long time.

1427
00:53:18,002 --> 00:53:19,602
- Really? - You look really tired today.

1428
00:53:19,842 --> 00:53:21,141
I wasn't able to get any sleep today.

1429
00:53:21,142 --> 00:53:22,911
- You look so tired. - I need a little bit of sleep.

1430
00:53:22,912 --> 00:53:24,041
Shouldn't you take a nap?

1431
00:53:24,042 --> 00:53:25,312
I wasn't able to have any tomato juice for a few days.

1432
00:53:25,612 --> 00:53:26,842
(Dumbfounded)

1433
00:53:27,582 --> 00:53:29,682
(The magical tomatoes...)

1434
00:53:29,812 --> 00:53:34,052
(are thrown into boiling water.)

1435
00:53:35,452 --> 00:53:36,552
Done.

1436
00:53:38,722 --> 00:53:40,561
Right. When they are thrown into cold water after that,

1437
00:53:40,562 --> 00:53:42,391
the peels will come off.

1438
00:53:42,392 --> 00:53:43,991
They can't be boiled for too long.

1439
00:53:43,992 --> 00:53:45,331
That will get rid of all of the vitamin C.

1440
00:53:45,332 --> 00:53:46,731
How long must they be blanched for?

1441
00:53:46,732 --> 00:53:48,701
- Around 2 to 3 minutes. - They are blanched.

1442
00:53:48,702 --> 00:53:50,401
Right. That's how the peels are removed.

1443
00:53:50,402 --> 00:53:53,142
(He carefully removes the peels for the important person.)

1444
00:53:56,912 --> 00:53:57,942
Should I slice them up a bit?

1445
00:54:00,542 --> 00:54:02,152
(Pressing)

1446
00:54:02,912 --> 00:54:04,982
(He struggles to cut it.)

1447
00:54:05,882 --> 00:54:07,382
The knife must be really blunt.

1448
00:54:07,452 --> 00:54:09,652
Is that so? Take this one.

1449
00:54:10,122 --> 00:54:12,262
It's fascinating.

1450
00:54:13,092 --> 00:54:15,062
That used to be the best knife.

1451
00:54:15,532 --> 00:54:17,262
But the knife that felt blunt worked well,

1452
00:54:17,762 --> 00:54:19,132
and the best knife felt blunt.

1453
00:54:19,732 --> 00:54:21,332
There's a bit of quantum dynamics.

1454
00:54:21,672 --> 00:54:23,371
- "Quantum dynamics?" - What are you saying?

1455
00:54:23,372 --> 00:54:24,602
(Dumbfounded)

1456
00:54:25,072 --> 00:54:26,502
- What's wrong? Did they fight? - Gosh.

1457
00:54:27,402 --> 00:54:29,742
I can't understand it as well. Did they get cursed?

1458
00:54:31,412 --> 00:54:32,682
(Putting in)

1459
00:54:32,942 --> 00:54:34,982
(He fills up the mixer with the tomatoes.)

1460
00:54:35,382 --> 00:54:36,581
(Pouring in yogurt)

1461
00:54:36,582 --> 00:54:38,451
- What is that? - So yogurt is added.

1462
00:54:38,452 --> 00:54:39,581
(A generous amount of olive oil)

1463
00:54:39,582 --> 00:54:41,552
- Olive oil? - It's really good.

1464
00:54:42,192 --> 00:54:45,092
(Shall I mix them up now?)

1465
00:54:45,562 --> 00:54:46,761
- That looks good. - Right.

1466
00:54:46,762 --> 00:54:47,762
It must be really good for the body.

1467
00:54:47,762 --> 00:54:48,762
That sweetens it up.

1468
00:54:50,532 --> 00:54:51,562
Is it ready?

1469
00:54:51,962 --> 00:54:53,902
- Gosh, it looks good. - Gosh.

1470
00:54:55,832 --> 00:54:57,371
(I hope that person likes it.)

1471
00:54:57,372 --> 00:54:58,442
Abalone.

1472
00:55:00,202 --> 00:55:01,741
- It's good. - Is it?

1473
00:55:01,742 --> 00:55:04,141
This one seemed to be a favorite.

1474
00:55:04,142 --> 00:55:05,611
- Along with the perilla leaves. - Her kimchi...

1475
00:55:05,612 --> 00:55:07,282
and side dishes are really good.

1476
00:55:07,412 --> 00:55:09,211
- The anchovy jangajji looks good. - The anchovies.

1477
00:55:09,212 --> 00:55:11,411
- Gosh. I know how they taste. - How important is this person?

1478
00:55:11,412 --> 00:55:13,122
- They're packing so many things. - Who are they going to meet?

1479
00:55:14,382 --> 00:55:16,991
Mom, since the house looked empty,

1480
00:55:16,992 --> 00:55:18,921
- Yes? - I got this.

1481
00:55:18,922 --> 00:55:19,962
What is it?

1482
00:55:20,322 --> 00:55:21,362
A summer rug.

1483
00:55:21,832 --> 00:55:22,932
A summer rug?

1484
00:55:23,962 --> 00:55:26,632
Since you like plants,

1485
00:55:27,402 --> 00:55:28,632
I got the deep green color.

1486
00:55:31,502 --> 00:55:35,072
The house looked empty after Coco's things were removed.

1487
00:55:35,472 --> 00:55:36,642
I wanted to help her make the house look less empty.

1488
00:55:36,742 --> 00:55:38,682
It feels quite empty without Coco.

1489
00:55:40,242 --> 00:55:43,382
After Coco crossed the Rainbow Bridge,

1490
00:55:43,882 --> 00:55:45,351
she struggled to get rid of Coco's things.

1491
00:55:45,352 --> 00:55:47,922
Gosh, why are so many dogs passing away?

1492
00:55:48,452 --> 00:55:49,951
In my mother's room,

1493
00:55:49,952 --> 00:55:52,592
there's Coco's urn,

1494
00:55:52,762 --> 00:55:56,561
snacks, and toys.

1495
00:55:56,562 --> 00:55:58,291
She left soon after Kkotbun left.

1496
00:55:58,292 --> 00:55:59,532
- Really? - Around two weeks later?

1497
00:55:59,962 --> 00:56:01,332
It was just around two weeks later.

1498
00:56:01,772 --> 00:56:03,602
I wanted to visit her often after that,

1499
00:56:04,072 --> 00:56:07,742
but she said she didn't want me to come.

1500
00:56:08,142 --> 00:56:12,182
She wanted to spend a few weeks with Coco.

1501
00:56:12,612 --> 00:56:15,112
- It must've been tough for her. - Right.

1502
00:56:15,552 --> 00:56:19,452
(Ju Seung and Coco had an intense relationship.)

1503
00:56:20,382 --> 00:56:24,022
(She looked comfortable with Ju Seung's mother.)

1504
00:56:25,122 --> 00:56:29,492
(Coco always followed her around.)

1505
00:56:30,932 --> 00:56:35,032
(Ju Seung's mother returned Coco with a greater love.)

1506
00:56:35,802 --> 00:56:38,272
This was what broke me heart even more.

1507
00:56:38,372 --> 00:56:40,872
His mom cooked for me to comfort my loss.

1508
00:56:41,002 --> 00:56:44,611
After the meal, I went, "Stay healthy, Coco."

1509
00:56:44,612 --> 00:56:46,411
- But she left after two weeks. - Gosh.

1510
00:56:46,412 --> 00:56:48,811
- Gosh. - I know how lonely...

1511
00:56:48,812 --> 00:56:50,981
- she would feel alone. - Right.

1512
00:56:50,982 --> 00:56:53,251
She must feel so lonely.

1513
00:56:53,252 --> 00:56:54,921
- Gosh. Poor thing. - Gosh.

1514
00:56:54,922 --> 00:56:56,291
(Coco left 12 years of joyful memories.)

1515
00:56:56,292 --> 00:56:59,022
Seeing Coco's photos after a while makes me feel...

1516
00:56:59,962 --> 00:57:01,222
I heard...

1517
00:57:01,462 --> 00:57:05,532
- my mother carried Coco's urn... - Gosh.

1518
00:57:05,832 --> 00:57:09,102
and went to the same places they went to for a walk.

1519
00:57:09,672 --> 00:57:12,171
This feeling will last for a while.

1520
00:57:12,172 --> 00:57:14,402
It won't disappear easily.

1521
00:57:17,042 --> 00:57:19,342
It isn't a slippery type of material.

1522
00:57:19,882 --> 00:57:21,712
It will flatten out over time.

1523
00:57:22,782 --> 00:57:24,711
Gosh, my legs!

1524
00:57:24,712 --> 00:57:25,852
(Let's try sitting on it.)

1525
00:57:26,252 --> 00:57:27,582
Can dogs step on this?

1526
00:57:28,052 --> 00:57:29,521
- Dogs can step on it. - She must...

1527
00:57:29,522 --> 00:57:30,821
- want to raise another dog. - Right.

1528
00:57:30,822 --> 00:57:32,322
She's thinking about it.

1529
00:57:32,492 --> 00:57:34,321
She's been talking about it quite a lot these days.

1530
00:57:34,322 --> 00:57:36,531
I saw Kian84's adoption as well.

1531
00:57:36,532 --> 00:57:38,231
(Dalkong, Alkong)

1532
00:57:38,232 --> 00:57:40,431
- Right. - My parents also went through...

1533
00:57:40,432 --> 00:57:41,902
- a pet loss. - Right.

1534
00:57:42,002 --> 00:57:44,471
Sunmoo is being a great son now.

1535
00:57:44,472 --> 00:57:45,501
Right.

1536
00:57:45,502 --> 00:57:47,142
I think it would be great for her to visit the adoption center.

1537
00:57:47,272 --> 00:57:48,471
- Right. - Let's go together.

1538
00:57:48,472 --> 00:57:50,171
- That sounds good. My mother... - You should go together.

