(Sitting alone in an empty room)

1957
01:16:34,753 --> 01:16:38,153
(Staring at the photo of his grandpa)

1958
01:16:40,793 --> 01:16:43,593
I really thought my grandpa was watching me.

1959
01:16:47,403 --> 01:16:48,833
I felt like I'd cry,

1960
01:16:50,473 --> 01:16:52,503
so I talked with him in my heart.

1961
01:16:53,443 --> 01:16:55,073
I spent time with him like that.

1962
01:16:57,173 --> 01:16:59,812
It's a shame, but if I think that he's watching over me,

1963
01:16:59,813 --> 01:17:01,683
- it consoles me a bit. - Right.

1964
01:17:09,023 --> 01:17:13,023
It'd have been nice if he saw it in person.

1965
01:17:19,603 --> 01:17:22,063
This is my one and only regret.

1966
01:17:22,203 --> 01:17:25,103
- What is it? - When I first got into music,

1967
01:17:25,403 --> 01:17:27,373
both my grandpa and grandma passed away.

1968
01:17:28,203 --> 01:17:31,112
I couldn't show them what I achieved...

1969
01:17:31,113 --> 01:17:32,613
- in my career. - Right.

1970
01:17:32,913 --> 01:17:35,082
- It must be a big regret. - They were really worried...

1971
01:17:35,083 --> 01:17:36,753
because I always wore torn pants.

1972
01:17:37,513 --> 01:17:39,152
- They'd sew it. - Grandmas always stitch them up.

1973
01:17:39,153 --> 01:17:41,022
- She'd tell me to pull my pants up. - She'd stitch them up with effort.

1974
01:17:41,023 --> 01:17:42,952
They must've wondered what I'd become when I grew up.

1975
01:17:42,953 --> 01:17:43,993
Of course.

1976
01:17:45,123 --> 01:17:48,723
(Massaging)

1977
01:17:52,063 --> 01:17:53,633
