- There are pockets too. - What?

1994
01:18:29,403 --> 01:18:30,502
There are pockets.

1995
01:18:30,503 --> 01:18:31,832
You can't live without pockets.

1996
01:18:31,833 --> 01:18:33,473
She got up to show.

1997
01:18:34,803 --> 01:18:36,112
She's serious about her style.

1998
01:18:36,113 --> 01:18:37,843
(Do you want to see the pockets?)

1999
01:18:38,173 --> 01:18:39,342
She's happy.

2000
01:18:39,343 --> 01:18:40,813
- It's nice. - It looks like wings.

2001
01:18:41,213 --> 01:18:43,083
It looks like a cactus too.

2002
01:18:43,113 --> 01:18:44,682
- It's quite hip. - It looks like a cactus too.

2003
01:18:44,683 --> 01:18:46,622
- The pockets... - It looks like a flower too.

2004
01:18:46,623 --> 01:18:48,952
- Yes. - It's fascinating.

2005
01:18:48,953 --> 01:18:51,553
- That's why I like it. - It's wonderful.

2006
01:18:52,253 --> 01:18:54,062
You look even more amazing standing up.

2007
01:18:54,063 --> 01:18:55,162
Your mother is trying hard.

2008
01:18:55,163 --> 01:18:56,293
You can't see it when you're seated.

2009
01:18:56,533 --> 01:18:58,793
- Because I was seated. - It's all black.

2010
01:18:58,893 --> 01:18:59,933
Yes.

2011
01:19:01,063 --> 01:19:02,873
- It looks expensive. - My goodness.

2012
01:19:03,173 --> 01:19:05,003
It was 500 dollars after the discount.

2013
01:19:05,633 --> 01:19:06,942
It's expensive even after the discount.

2014
01:19:06,943 --> 01:19:08,872
She always mentions the price.

2015
01:19:08,873 --> 01:19:10,612
- They always mention it. - That's what elders do.

2016
01:19:10,613 --> 01:19:12,113
- Every time. - It's important.

2017
01:19:12,343 --> 01:19:13,783
My nose looks exactly like yours.

2018
01:19:14,183 --> 01:19:16,183
People keep saying that I got a nose job.

2019
01:19:16,283 --> 01:19:17,613
But I take after your nose.

2020
01:19:17,883 --> 01:19:18,952
What did you say?

2021
01:19:18,953 --> 01:19:21,583
My nose looks like yours, right?

2022
01:19:22,083 --> 01:19:23,853
- You're right. - So is that bad?

2023
01:19:24,123 --> 01:19:26,592
No, people ask me if I got a nose job.

2024
01:19:26,593 --> 01:19:28,193
A nose job? I see.

2025
01:19:28,723 --> 01:19:30,193
- Your nose... - They say my nose...

2026
01:19:30,463 --> 01:19:31,533
keeps getting bigger.

2027
01:19:31,693 --> 01:19:33,162
My nose has always gotten bigger.

2028
01:19:33,163 --> 01:19:36,032
It'd be better if your face got wider.

2029
01:19:36,033 --> 01:19:37,702
- If my face got wider? - If your face got bigger...

2030
01:19:37,703 --> 01:19:39,103
(My face getting wider?)

2031
01:19:39,203 --> 01:19:40,573
- If his face gets wider? - It's okay.

2032
01:19:40,703 --> 01:19:42,303
- Is it? - Yes, it's pretty.

2033
01:19:42,743 --> 01:19:44,313
He's pretty because he's my grandson.

2034
01:19:44,413 --> 01:19:45,913
- Of course. - Ju Seung is handsome.

2035
01:19:46,083 --> 01:19:47,742
He has a lucky nose.

2036
01:19:47,743 --> 01:19:49,512
It does seem like your nose got bigger.

2037
01:19:49,513 --> 01:19:51,252
- Is that why he's called CORTIS? - My nose keeps getting bigger.

2038
01:19:51,253 --> 01:19:52,382
Yes, it's CORTIS.

2039
01:19:52,383 --> 01:19:54,183
- My nose is the only thing you see. - That's...

2040
01:19:54,453 --> 01:19:56,093
You keep mentioning CORTIS.

2041
01:19:56,493 --> 01:19:58,992
- Just call yourself BIGNOSETIS. - It's way bigger now.

2042
01:19:58,993 --> 01:20:00,393
BIGNOSETIS?

2043
01:20:00,423 --> 01:20:02,022
- BIGNOSETIS. - How could you call him BIGNOSETIS?

2044
01:20:02,023 --> 01:20:03,532
That's so weird.

2045
01:20:03,533 --> 01:20:04,933
BIGNOSETIS.

2046
01:20:05,563 --> 01:20:07,132
He's so witty.

2047
01:20:07,133 --> 01:20:08,603
- That's right. - Of course.

2048
01:20:09,203 --> 01:20:13,243
When I wake up, I do this 50 times.

2049
01:20:13,673 --> 01:20:15,742
Then do this 50 times.

2050
01:20:15,743 --> 01:20:17,172
I do this 50 times.

2051
01:20:17,173 --> 01:20:18,672
And do 50 times here.

2052
01:20:18,673 --> 01:20:20,642
Do this 50 times.

2053
01:20:20,643 --> 01:20:22,813
- So she massages her face. - I do this.

2054
01:20:23,013 --> 01:20:24,152
- Really? - All my face.

2055
01:20:24,153 --> 01:20:25,352
Of course. She does it every day.

2056
01:20:25,353 --> 01:20:26,423
Why didn't you tell me?

2057
01:20:26,523 --> 01:20:28,422
- How do you do it? Tell me again. - She does it for 40 minutes.

2058
01:20:28,423 --> 01:20:29,753
- Here? - No.

2059
01:20:29,853 --> 01:20:31,992
- Grab your eyebrows... - My eyebrows.

2060
01:20:31,993 --> 01:20:32,993
while lying down.

2061
01:20:32,994 --> 01:20:35,423
- Swipe them 50 times. - Do this 50 times.

2062
01:20:35,793 --> 01:20:38,093
- Then do this 50 times. - Do this 50 times.

2063
01:20:38,693 --> 01:20:40,532
Then do this 50 times too.

2064
01:20:40,533 --> 01:20:43,673
Is that why my nose got big?

2065
01:20:44,473 --> 01:20:46,373
Her nose got big indeed.

2066
01:20:46,403 --> 01:20:49,042
- Then press here. - Press it.

2067
01:20:49,043 --> 01:20:52,413
Then lift your face like this.

2068
01:20:52,513 --> 01:20:54,182
- Then do this. - Okay.

2069
01:20:54,183 --> 01:20:56,912
Do this, and you'll get fewer wrinkles on your neck.

2070
01:20:56,913 --> 01:20:58,512
With the massages, I have no problem.

2071
01:20:58,513 --> 01:20:59,622
Like this?

2072
01:20:59,623 --> 01:21:01,083
Like this? Push it up?

2073
01:21:01,223 --> 01:21:03,122
You're the original meridian massage therapist.

2074
01:21:03,123 --> 01:21:04,153
Like this.

2075
01:21:04,623 --> 01:21:06,422
Elders know that stuff the best.

2076
01:21:06,423 --> 01:21:09,592
I do arm exercises too. I do everything for an hour.

2077
01:21:09,593 --> 01:21:10,662
(He manages to put her in a better mood...)

2078
01:21:10,663 --> 01:21:11,733
(and learns massaging tips.)

2079
01:21:11,833 --> 01:21:13,832
The weather is amazing today, Grandma.

2080
01:21:13,833 --> 01:21:15,302
- It's a relief. - It's perfect to walk...

2081
01:21:15,303 --> 01:21:16,873
since there's not much sunlight.

2082
01:21:17,673 --> 01:21:18,802
The day's great.

2083
01:21:18,803 --> 01:21:20,403
Shall we get some air?

2084
01:21:20,873 --> 01:21:21,943
Is it okay?

2085
01:21:22,973 --> 01:21:24,313
I need to put this on.

2086
01:21:25,473 --> 01:21:27,112
- Since it's cold... - She's stylish.

2087
01:21:27,113 --> 01:21:30,013
Gosh, she put on a beautiful scarf.

2088
01:21:30,383 --> 01:21:32,413
Grandma, what about a hat? Aren't you going to put on one?

2089
01:21:32,753 --> 01:21:34,082
- A hat? - Put this on.

2090
01:21:34,083 --> 01:21:35,522
- The hat is there? - This...

2091
01:21:35,523 --> 01:21:36,622
- That's... - It's perfect.

2092
01:21:36,623 --> 01:21:38,053
(Putting it on)

2093
01:21:38,253 --> 01:21:39,323
She's indeed a Seongsu person.

2094
01:21:39,893 --> 01:21:41,193
She's so stylish.

2095
01:21:41,463 --> 01:21:43,292
- I knew it. - It goes really well.

2096
01:21:43,293 --> 01:21:45,392
- It's so nice. - You look way better with this.

2097
01:21:45,393 --> 01:21:46,403
That's right.

2098
01:21:47,303 --> 01:21:50,133
Going out for a walk could be an exercise,

2099
01:21:50,273 --> 01:21:52,133
but I wanted them...

2100
01:21:52,733 --> 01:21:54,503
to get rid of old emotions.

2101
01:21:55,103 --> 01:21:57,913
I thought it'd be nice to go for a walk together,

2102
01:21:58,173 --> 01:21:59,312
so that's why we went.

2103
01:21:59,313 --> 01:22:00,412
(They go out for a walk to refresh themselves.)

2104
01:22:00,413 --> 01:22:02,113
- You look great now. - Right.

2105
01:22:02,713 --> 01:22:06,083
- It's the best. - Your outfit is amazing, Mother.

2106
01:22:06,253 --> 01:22:08,923
I'll be right back. Take care of the house.

2107
01:22:09,653 --> 01:22:11,093
Goodness.

2108
01:22:11,823 --> 01:22:14,863
(She doesn't forget to say goodbye before going out.)

2109
01:22:15,463 --> 01:22:16,563
Grandma, what shoes are you wearing?

2110
01:22:16,833 --> 01:22:18,432
Are you wearing these? The ones that look like rubber shoes?

2111
01:22:18,433 --> 01:22:19,933
- Is that okay? - Yes.

2112
01:22:21,503 --> 01:22:23,272
I can't wear platform shoes.

2113
01:22:23,273 --> 01:22:25,673
I only wear these, so they look worn out.

2114
01:22:26,173 --> 01:22:27,173
All set.

2115
01:22:28,003 --> 01:22:29,203
Gosh, thank you.

2116
01:22:31,613 --> 01:22:34,313
- My gosh. - Let's get some air...

2117
01:22:35,113 --> 01:22:36,253
and refresh ourselves.

2118
01:22:40,553 --> 01:22:42,953
(Full of excitement)

2119
01:22:43,823 --> 01:22:45,152
(They go out, feeling excited.)

2120
01:22:45,153 --> 01:22:46,293
They're so cool.

2121
01:22:46,563 --> 01:22:48,392
- Ju Seung, you're amazing. - He's amazing.

2122
01:22:48,393 --> 01:22:49,422
- It's amazing. - You could've changed your car.

2123
01:22:49,423 --> 01:22:51,162
- Seriously. - I know.

2124
01:22:51,163 --> 01:22:52,363
(He's more incredible, the more I think about it.)

2125
01:22:53,833 --> 01:22:55,532
Grandma, we're here.

2126
01:22:55,533 --> 01:22:56,933
(They've arrived at a place to take a walk.)

2127
01:22:59,073 --> 01:23:00,403
(Taking it out)

2128
01:23:00,473 --> 01:23:02,143
The sun isn't that strong, but still...

2129
01:23:02,913 --> 01:23:03,973
I'll hold it for you.

2130
01:23:06,173 --> 01:23:07,212
Take your time.

2131
01:23:07,213 --> 01:23:09,143
(As soon as Grandma gets out,)

2132
01:23:09,443 --> 01:23:10,952
(he puts up the sun umbrella.)

2133
01:23:10,953 --> 01:23:12,883
Grandma, be careful. You can't use the cane here.

2134
01:23:12,953 --> 01:23:14,283
- Goodness. - You can't use the cane here.

2135
01:23:15,423 --> 01:23:18,022
Grandma, you walk better than usual today.

2136
01:23:18,023 --> 01:23:20,162
It must be because I'm happy.

2137
01:23:20,163 --> 01:23:21,662
- You did well. - She walks well.

2138
01:23:21,663 --> 01:23:24,733
They sprinkled water here because it's too hot.

2139
01:23:26,063 --> 01:23:28,633
(A perfect course for his grandma where it's easy to walk)

2140
01:23:29,573 --> 01:23:30,633
The flowers are pretty here.

2141
01:23:31,003 --> 01:23:32,033
Goodness.

2142
01:23:33,403 --> 01:23:35,073
Gosh, how pretty.

2143
01:23:35,243 --> 01:23:36,542
Grandma is still like a little girl.

2144
01:23:36,543 --> 01:23:39,073
She likes flowers and pretty things.

2145
01:23:40,883 --> 01:23:44,313
(Rummaging)

2146
01:23:45,253 --> 01:23:46,622
I should take a photo with my camera.

2147
01:23:46,623 --> 01:23:47,883
- Mom, hold this for me. - Photos?

2148
01:23:50,293 --> 01:23:51,492
How nice.

2149
01:23:51,493 --> 01:23:52,822
Gosh, Director Lee.

2150
01:23:52,823 --> 01:23:54,993
He looks different now even with just a camera.

2151
01:23:55,463 --> 01:23:57,632
You guys changed because he won first place.

2152
01:23:57,633 --> 01:23:59,362
- Gosh. - It makes me see him with bias.

2153
01:23:59,363 --> 01:24:00,663
He's so biased.

2154
01:24:01,803 --> 01:24:03,473
Is this also that flower?

2155
01:24:05,173 --> 01:24:06,772
It looks like Monet's painting.

2156
01:24:06,773 --> 01:24:08,273
(Grandma being happy)

2157
01:24:08,773 --> 01:24:10,142
- There are thorns. - Don't touch them.

2158
01:24:10,143 --> 01:24:11,172
(Director Lee doesn't miss a moment.)

2159
01:24:11,173 --> 01:24:12,872
She touches all the flowers.

2160
01:24:12,873 --> 01:24:14,842
There are fewer thorns. This doesn't have one.

2161
01:24:14,843 --> 01:24:16,042
(Ju Seung's camera)

2162
01:24:16,043 --> 01:24:17,783
Gosh, the shot looks different because he's a director.

2163
01:24:18,253 --> 01:24:19,852
- Seriously. - That's prejudiced.

2164
01:24:19,853 --> 01:24:21,522
Hyun Moo, I had the exact same thought.

2165
01:24:21,523 --> 01:24:22,993
I was going to say it, but you said it first.

2166
01:24:23,093 --> 01:24:24,192
You were too late.

2167
01:24:24,193 --> 01:24:25,753
How did he come up with that shot?

2168
01:24:26,423 --> 01:24:28,122
Have you gone mad?

2169
01:24:28,123 --> 01:24:30,433
- It's so different. - Gosh, Kian84.

2170
01:24:31,063 --> 01:24:33,362
He already has a storyboard in his head.

2171
01:24:33,363 --> 01:24:34,562
- With a handheld camera... - I'm envious.

2172
01:24:34,563 --> 01:24:37,203
- His hands don't even shake. - The flowers are brought to life.

2173
01:24:38,903 --> 01:24:41,202
(She sits on the bench with the help of a master director.)

2174
01:24:41,203 --> 01:24:42,273
Goodness.

2175
01:24:42,873 --> 01:24:44,712
- You're walking a lot today. - How tiring.

2176
01:24:44,713 --> 01:24:46,443
You walk so well. You're like you're in your 60s.

2177
01:24:47,113 --> 01:24:48,783
It's because I'm so happy.

2178
01:24:49,283 --> 01:24:51,183
- How nice. - She's become a little girl.

2179
01:24:53,223 --> 01:24:54,253
Look.

2180
01:24:54,383 --> 01:24:56,493
Think of it as the sea. Look over there.

2181
01:24:57,523 --> 01:24:58,953
"Dear sea."

2182
01:25:00,163 --> 01:25:02,523
"Take good care of my husband."

2183
01:25:03,433 --> 01:25:05,763
(A little wish she offers from afar)

2184
01:25:06,033 --> 01:25:08,532
Do you think it'll get better after Grandpa's birthday?

2185
01:25:08,533 --> 01:25:10,573
Yes, I think it'll get better.

2186
01:25:12,573 --> 01:25:15,272
What if it gets better after a year?

2187
01:25:15,273 --> 01:25:17,843
A bird is coming to us.

2188
01:25:20,343 --> 01:25:22,043
- You're right. - A bird is coming to us.

2189
01:25:22,643 --> 01:25:23,882
- Come here. - Goodness.

2190
01:25:23,883 --> 01:25:25,053
(A sparrow approaches Ju Seung's family.)

2191
01:25:25,683 --> 01:25:26,922
Did he become a bird?

2192
01:25:26,923 --> 01:25:28,123
(Did my husband become a bird?)

2193
01:25:28,223 --> 01:25:29,253
Goodness.

2194
01:25:30,653 --> 01:25:34,093
Gosh, it's nice to be out.

2195
01:25:35,123 --> 01:25:36,392
Let's come out more often.

2196
01:25:36,393 --> 01:25:37,592
(A Wonderful Day Made Better by Being Together)

2197
01:25:37,593 --> 01:25:39,493
The Han River is close by.

2198
01:25:40,463 --> 01:25:41,963
(Next story)

2199
01:25:42,803 --> 01:25:45,803
(Proved his presence with his unique sense of style)

2200
01:25:46,303 --> 01:25:48,673
(A skilled musician who transcends genres)

2201
01:25:49,273 --> 01:25:51,412
(Hello.)

2202
01:25:51,413 --> 01:25:53,583
(It's been 4 years since I started living alone.)

2203
01:25:53,783 --> 01:25:55,483
(Singer DAWN)

2204
01:25:57,053 --> 01:25:59,923
(He starts his morning by opening the windows.)

2205
01:26:00,923 --> 01:26:03,953
(A 2-story house welcomed by a small yard)

2206
01:26:04,323 --> 01:26:05,622
(My house...)

2207
01:26:05,623 --> 01:26:07,193
(is almost like a museum.)

2208
01:26:07,623 --> 01:26:09,733
(Preserving the original elements...)

2209
01:26:10,193 --> 01:26:12,292
(while adding an Eastern aesthetic)

2210
01:26:12,293 --> 01:26:14,703
There are many objects inspired by intangible cultural heritage.

2211
01:26:15,163 --> 01:26:17,232
(A space filled with items of his taste)

2212
01:26:17,233 --> 01:26:19,373
I like placing the items I like nonchalantly.

2213
01:26:20,643 --> 01:26:22,743
(DAWN house with Haetnim, his dog)

2214
01:26:23,343 --> 01:26:25,243
(He enjoys brunch while sitting on the front porch.)

2215
01:26:25,713 --> 01:26:27,243
(Slow)

2216
01:26:29,083 --> 01:26:31,053
(He's slower than a sloth.)

2217
01:26:32,383 --> 01:26:36,453
(How leisurely and peaceful it is.)

2218
01:26:37,423 --> 01:26:39,253
(I have my own pace.)

2219
01:26:39,523 --> 01:26:41,623
(Sipping peace today as well)

2220
01:26:42,923 --> 01:26:44,262
(Puttering around)

2221
01:26:44,263 --> 01:26:45,993
(A meditation continued through the touch of his hands)

2222
01:26:46,963 --> 01:26:49,233
(Not dwelling on misfortunes,)

2223
01:26:50,603 --> 01:26:52,633
(but simply enjoying the peace of hearing no news)

2224
01:26:55,073 --> 01:26:56,643
(What do I do?)

2225
01:26:56,913 --> 01:27:01,243
(A peace that's suddenly shaken)

2226
01:27:02,683 --> 01:27:06,213
(A Simple Day)

2227
01:27:07,123 --> 01:27:08,823
(For the crew members who got hungry after running,)

2228
01:27:09,123 --> 01:27:10,993
(the cooking chief gets to work.)

2229
01:27:11,323 --> 01:27:12,553
(1st round, cold pork slices)

2230
01:27:13,163 --> 01:27:14,623
(That must be really delicious.)

2231
01:27:14,723 --> 01:27:16,422
(Cold pork slices...)

2232
01:27:16,423 --> 01:27:17,433
(must be delicious.)

2233
01:27:18,033 --> 01:27:19,763
(2nd round will be carbs.)

2234
01:27:21,103 --> 01:27:22,133
Gosh, that must be delicious.

2235
01:27:24,133 --> 01:27:25,373
(Teary-eyed)

2236
01:27:26,003 --> 01:27:27,903
(Now we are talking.)

2237
01:27:28,573 --> 01:27:30,643
(It's time to become one with a team name.)

2238
01:27:31,013 --> 01:27:32,173
(Let's call ourselves this.)

2239
01:27:32,843 --> 01:27:34,313
(You're indeed a crew leader.)

2240
01:27:34,813 --> 01:27:36,883
(Cheers to us who will run together!)

2241
01:27:37,653 --> 01:27:39,983
(The affection they have built for each other through time together)

2242
01:27:40,253 --> 01:27:42,053
(I'm always watching others.)

2243
01:27:42,353 --> 01:27:44,623
(I can totally see you taking care of us.)

2244
01:27:44,793 --> 01:27:47,193
(He feels bad for Kian84 who always blames himself.)

2245
01:27:47,563 --> 01:27:49,393
(It's because I became soft-hearted.)

2246
01:27:50,133 --> 01:27:51,793
(That's why I want to be with you even more.)

2247
01:27:56,303 --> 01:27:59,843
(A Friendship Sweeter than Sweat)
